1 NOTE Son of [[bocklandt_edouard_1839]] and [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]], and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]]'s brother.
2 CONT His marriage act — Diksmuide nr. 40, 11 February 1893
2 CONT ([[agatha-diksmuide-1893-marriage-bocklandt-vincke]]) — names him born at Hamme 2 July
2 CONT 1867, *koordedraaier* (ropemaker — his father's own trade under a different word), resident
2 CONT at Oostende, son of Eduard Bocklandt (53, *koordedraaier*) and the already-deceased Maria
2 CONT Louisa Vanbergen. He married **Florence Amelie Vincke** (b. Diksmuide 22 Apr 1869,
2 CONT *kantwerkster*), daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] of Diksmuide — now
2 CONT her own record, [[vincke_florence_1869]]. AGATHA serves this act only as an "analyse van akte"
2 CONT (index transcription), not the register image, hence `sup`.
2 CONT
2 CONT RESOLVED (research-log §64). This act was previously flagged as a frontier: the bride's
2 CONT parents shared full names with this tree's existing [[vincke_lucien_1840]] x [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]
2 CONT (parents of [[vincke_emma_1880]], Van Iseghem line), but the act alone named them by name only —
2 CONT one identifier, not the two a graft needs — and Florence Amelie had no record of her own to
2 CONT graft onto. With her own record now written, a province-wide sweep of the Diksmuide birth
2 CONT index found no rival couple of that name, so the link stands: this marriage joins the Van
2 CONT Iseghem and De Keyser/Bocklandt branches of this tree (objective 3).
