1 FAMC @F8@
1 NOTE Father of Louise Marie Bocklandt (1877, Hamme O-Vl). Born 1839 at Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen);
2 CONT married Maria Louisa Van Bergen (1842-1888). Died Oostende 4 July 1907.
2 CONT
2 CONT CITATION REPAIRED (2026-07-26), replacing the §52 downgrade. Two acts now stand behind this
2 CONT record. His own death act — Oostende nr. 417, 4 July 1907
2 CONT ([[agatha-oostende-1907-death-eduardus-bocklandt]]) — names his parents **Antonius
2 CONT Dominicus Bocklandt** and **Isabella Livina Ichau** (both already deceased, place not
2 CONT stated), independently of the wete1998 tree that first supplied them, and gives his death
2 CONT date and Hamme birthplace. The act spells her **Isabella Livina**, against this record's
2 CONT **Isabella Livia** — a single-letter variant, and with no rival Isabella Ichau anywhere in
2 CONT the record to collide with, so it is read as the same woman; the same note is on
2 CONT [[ichau_isabella_1803]]'s own record. The Hamme death act of his young son Ludovicus, 9 June
2 CONT 1880 — register image read directly ([[fs-hamme-1880-death-ludovicus-bocklandt]]) — puts
2 CONT him at Hamme with Maria Louisa Van Bergen, aged 40 (consistent with the held birth of
2 CONT 1839), trade *zeeldraaier* (ropemaker).
2 CONT
2 CONT CONFIDENCE STAYS `sup`, not `doc`. The parent-link fact — his own parentage — rests on the
2 CONT 1907 death act, and AGATHA serves that act only as an "analyse van akte" (a volunteer index
2 CONT transcription); the image itself sits behind an AGATHA login and was not opened. The 1880
2 CONT register image WAS read, but it does not name his own parents, so it cannot carry that
2 CONT particular fact to `doc` on its own.
2 CONT
2 CONT Six more of his and Maria Louisa's children now have their own records, each sourced to an
2 CONT act naming him by name as father: [[bocklandt_paulina_1870]] (m. Oostende 1888),
2 CONT [[bocklandt_maria_1874]] (m. Oostende 1892), [[bocklandt_maria_1872]] (m. Oostende 1893),
2 CONT [[bocklandt_caesar_1867]] (m. Diksmuide 1893), [[bocklandt_philemondus_1880]] (m. Oostende 1900) and
2 CONT [[bocklandt_alphonsus]] (d. Oostende 1892), alongside [[bocklandt_ludovicus_1875]] (d. Hamme
2 CONT 1880) and [[bocklandt_louise_1877]] herself. Across the four marriage acts of 1888-1900 he is
2 CONT consistently *touwslagersknecht* (a ropemaker's assistant) at Oostende — the same trade as
2 CONT *zeeldraaier* at Hamme in 1880, under a different word for it — and his stated age rises
2 CONT from 50 (1888) to 62 (1900), which fits a birth of 1838-1839 throughout.
1 SOUR @S10@
2 QUAY 2
