1 REFN bocklandt_louise_1877
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Louise Marie /Bocklandt/
2 GIVN Louise Marie
2 SURN Bocklandt
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 31 DEC 1877
2 PLAC Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 JUL 1946
2 PLAC Oostende
1 FAMS @F5@
1 FAMS @F10@
1 FAMC @F6@
1 NOTE Source detail: Stene marriage act nr. 9, 1 March 1924 (FamilySearch register image, read
2 CONT directly — [[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]]); Familiekunde Westkust memorial
2 CONT card ([[S17]]); Geneanet tree wete1998 (Erik Bekaert, for the ancestors above her parents).
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 31 Dec 1877 in Hamme (OOST-VLAANDEREN, Waasland) — the SAME town as her first husband
2 CONT Édouard Dekeyser (both Hamme natives who moved to Oostende). This is the true source of the
2 CONT long 'Hamme' confusion: it was the couple's shared birth-town, not Hamme-Merchtem and not a
2 CONT marriage place. Married Édouard 4 May 1901 (the marriage legitimized their two eldest
2 CONT children); they DIVORCED on 14 November 1922, by decree of the Rechtbank van eersten aanleg
2 CONT te Brugge. Died 1946 Oostende, buried at Stene. Her Bocklandt family is a Hamme (O-Vl) /
2 CONT Waasland family documented back to the 1760s (see her parents and the Bocklandt / Van
2 CONT Bergen ancestors).
2 CONT
2 CONT SHE REMARRIED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Westkust memorial-card record ([[S17]]) gives her
2 CONT death as **15 July 1946 at Oostende** — the tree had only the year — with her birthplace
2 CONT Hamme, and names her partner as **Petrus Blomme**.
2 CONT
2 CONT Not Édouard. She and [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]] divorced in 1922, and this is the first sign of what
2 CONT she did afterwards: she married again. The chronology is quietly striking — Édouard
2 CONT remarried Leontine Schreel at Oostende on 9 May 1946, and Louise died nine weeks later, on
2 CONT 15 July, a Blomme.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUND (2026-07-26), closing the frontier this record used to carry. The Bocklandt–Blomme
2 CONT marriage act itself: Stene, 1 March 1924, akte nr. 9, register image read directly
2 CONT ([[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]]). She is a *werkvrouw*, born Hamme 31 December
2 CONT 1877 — exact to the day and to the commune — daughter of Eduardus Bocklandt (d. Oostende
2 CONT 4 Jul 1907) and Maria Louisa Van Den Bergen (d. Oostende 22 Nov 1888), and the act states in
2 CONT full that she is the *gescheiden echtgenoote* of Eduardus De Keyser, divorced by the
2 CONT Rechtbank van eersten aanleg te Brugge on 14 November 1922 — dating the divorce this record
2 CONT had only as `~1923`. The groom, [[blomme_petrus_1884]], is given as *werkman*, born Stene 23
2 CONT January 1884, son of Josephus Blomme (living, Oostende) and Mathilde Sophia Meseure (d.
2 CONT Oostende 21 Jul 1922).
2 CONT
2 CONT A TRAP FOR THE NEXT READER. FamilySearch's own index dates this act **1 May 1924**. The
2 CONT register itself reads *"den eersten Maart"* — 1 March — confirmed by the facing act (nr. 8,
2 CONT 23 February 1924) and by the banns, published Sunday 10 February 1924: neither fits a May
2 CONT wedding. The index's own raw month field reads `"Maand": "Maa"`, which the site auto-expands
2 CONT to the English "May" instead of the Dutch "Maart" — a demonstrable indexing bug, not a
2 CONT second date to reconcile. The register, not the index, is what is cited here.
2 CONT
2 CONT RESTORED (2026-07-26) to `doc`. §52 downgraded this record because its only citation was a
2 CONT bare `agatha` — no page id, no artifact, no search-log entry, so `doc` could not be checked
2 CONT against anything. That gap is closed: the citation is now the register image itself
2 CONT ([[fs-stene-1924-marriage-blomme-bocklandt]], an artifact saved from the FamilySearch
2 CONT viewer), and it carries two identifiers independent of the wete1998 tree that first
2 CONT supplied her parents — her birth exact to the day and commune, and the De Keyser
2 CONT marriage-and-divorce, itself independently corroborated by [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s own 1946
2 CONT remarriage act, read 22 years later.
1 SOUR @S11@
2 QUAY 3
