2 CONT (index transcription), not the register image, hence `sup`.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Hamme just two days after his infant brother [[bocklandt_ludovicus_1875]] died in the
2 CONT same town — 10 June against 8 June 1880. That is close enough to read the marriage act's
2 CONT birthdate with some caution: it is a date recalled twenty years later, not a contemporary
2 CONT record, and the true gap between the two events may not be quite this narrow.
