1 REFN bogaert_petronilla
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Petronilla /Bogaert/
2 GIVN Petronilla
2 SURN Bogaert
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1711
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1792
2 NOTE Recorded as: buried 31 August 1792 at Evergem
1 FAMS @F12@
1 FAMC @F11@
1 NOTE Wife of [[bundervoet_christoffel_1709]], and the mother of the line: their son
2 CONT [[bundervoet_philippus_1756]] is the direct ancestor of Renée and Léon.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The Evergem burial register of 1792 supplies almost everything this record used to
2 CONT lack.** It held a bare `death: 1792` from the fauconier parenteel and nothing else — no
2 CONT birth, no parents. The register entry gives her burial on **31 August 1792**, a birth year
2 CONT of **1711**, and her own parents, [[bogaert_petrus]] and [[taedts_maria]] — a generation
2 CONT the tree did not have at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two independent identifiers licence the join: the death year 1792, which the held record
2 CONT already carried from a different source, and the husband, named in the register as
2 CONT Christophorus Bundervoet.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The date is the burial, not the death.** The register gives no date of death, so the year
2 CONT stands as the fact and the day of burial sits beside it in `raw` rather than being
2 CONT collapsed into a death date the source never stated. The same distinction her
2 CONT brother-in-law's record draws — see [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]], buried at Assenede in 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT Read from the FamilySearch index entry, not from the register image, so `sup` throughout.
2 CONT Reading the image would give the burial in the parish's own words, and might name a
2 CONT widower — which would date [[bundervoet_christoffel_1709]]'s death against the 1786 the
2 CONT tree holds.
1 SOUR @S17@
