2 PLAC Kraainem
1 OCCU landbouwer (farmer)
1 FAMS @F16@
1 FAMC @F14@
1 NOTE CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father, by his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of
2 CONT 20 June 1872, which names the bride's parents as Guilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina
2 CONT Peremans.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026): named in his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 as
2 CONT *landbouwer*, living at Kraainem — an occupation this record did not have.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — Zaventem nr. 1, 24 February 1846 (S19),
2 CONT read as an image. He married [[peremans_joanna_1824]] there, and the act states he was **born at
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, was **21 years old**, and worked as an *arbeider*. The age puts his
2 CONT birth in 1824 or early 1825, confirming from a civil act the 1824 this record had carried
2 CONT from a member tree; the birthplace is new, and the *landbouwer* of 1872 was a labourer at
2 CONT twenty-one.
2 CONT
2 CONT It also names his parents, [[bossin_arnoldus]] and [[deyn_elisabeth]] of
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, both present at the wedding, both consenting, and neither able to
2 CONT write. They are recorded here from this act.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26): he appears again as a **witness at his sister's wedding** —
2 CONT [[bossin_anna_1829]], Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). The bride's
2 CONT parents are named identically to his own, and he is there in person, so this tree gains
2 CONT his sister and he gains a sibling.
2 CONT
2 CONT **It also dates him twice over.** He is **29** on 1 December 1853, which places his birth
2 CONT between December 1823 and December 1824; his own act made him **21** on 24 February 1846,
2 CONT which places it between February 1824 and February 1825. The two windows overlap only in
2 CONT **1824, between late February and early December** — two acts, seven years apart, agreeing
2 CONT on a year this record had been carrying from a member tree alone.
2 CONT
2 CONT His trade moves with him: *arbeider* at twenty-one, *steenslager* at twenty-nine,
2 CONT *landbouwer* of Kraainem by 1872. He was living at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, where he was born,
2 CONT in 1853.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
2 CONT
2 CONT A FOURTH CHILD (2026-07-27): [[bossin_joannes_1851]], a birth act at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr.
2 CONT 19, 15 August 1851 — a son between [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (1849) and [[bossin_ludovica_1853]] (1853). He
2 CONT self-declares on that act, aged 27, born Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *daglooner*.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Birth window narrowed again.** Age 27 on 15 August 1851 puts his own birth between 16
2 CONT August 1823 and 15 August 1824. Crossed against the window this record already carried —
2 CONT 25 February to 1 December 1824, from the 1846 marriage act and the 1853 witness
2 CONT appearance — the overlap narrows to **25 February – 15 August 1824**. The `birth.date`
2 CONT field stays `"1824"`: the date grammar's only span form is a year-to-year range
2 CONT (`1575..1587`), so a day-precision window cannot be written as the field itself, and a
2 CONT plain `"1824"` already asserts no more than the year, which both windows agree on. The
2 CONT narrower window is recorded here, in prose, as what the evidence now permits — not as a
2 CONT change to what the field asserts.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also appears again as father, self-declaring, aged 29, at [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s own
2 CONT birth act (Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 18, 5 October 1853, S33) — a *steenslager* there, same
2 CONT trade as his sister's 1853 witness appearance already gave him. That age falls inside the
2 CONT narrowed window with no conflict.
2 CONT
2 CONT A FIFTH AND SIXTH CHILD (2026-07-27): [[bossin_henricus_1863]] (b. Kraainem, 1 January 1863)
2 CONT and [[bossin_joannes_1866]] (b. Kraainem, 17 March 1866), found from Henricus's own
2 CONT 1887 Kraainem marriage act and Joannes Franciscus's own 1896 Werchter marriage act
2 CONT respectively — both name this couple as parents directly.
2 CONT
2 CONT **DEATH DATED TO THE DAY, and corroborated twice independently.** This record held only
2 CONT the year 1888. His daughter [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1901 Kraainem remarriage act and his
2 CONT son [[bossin_joannes_1866]]'s 1896 Werchter marriage act — two different children,
2 CONT two different registers, five years apart — both give his death as **Kraainem, 10
2 CONT October 1888**, agreeing to the day. That is what makes the day-level date safe to hold
2 CONT rather than a single-source guess, and it now supersedes the bare year.
2 CONT
2 CONT **UPGRADED BACK TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — two register images, not index rows, were read.**
2 CONT [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1884 Kraainem marriage act and [[bossin_henricus_1863]]'s 1887 Kraainem
2 CONT marriage act were both read as images. Both state him **present in person and
2 CONT consenting** alongside his wife [[peremans_joanna_1824]] — the 1887 act naming both explicitly:
2 CONT *"beiden alhier tegenwoordig en toestemmende."* That puts a **hard floor of 23 November
2 CONT 1887** under the 10 October 1888 death this record already holds, a third, direct
2 CONT confirmation independent of the two children's later acts that first supplied the
2 CONT day-level date. This does not reopen §52's downgrade of the AGATHA-only acts, which remain
2 CONT `sup`-grade evidence in their own right; it is these two specific, newly-read images that
2 CONT carry the record's overall confidence back to `doc`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **TWO MORE SONS-IN-LAW, NAMED BUT NOT LINKED — a frontier, not a graft.** Both weddings
2 CONT name a brother-in-law of the bride/groom whose own wife is never given: **Petrus
2 CONT Vanhoudenhoven**, aged 30 in 1884 and 34 in 1887 (b. ~1853), stated *schoonbroeder der
2 CONT bruid* at [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding and *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms* at
2 CONT [[bossin_henricus_1863]]'s — the same man both times, on the arithmetic — and **Egidius
2 CONT Franciscus De Hondt**, 26 in 1887 (b. ~1861), stated *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms* at
2 CONT [[bossin_henricus_1863]]'s wedding only. Each therefore married a Bossin daughter of this
2 CONT couple who is not yet identified in this tree — a seventh child, or an eighth, neither
2 CONT named in any register read so far. Recorded here, once, rather than duplicated on every
2 CONT child's own page.
