1 REFN bossin_henricus_1863
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Henricus /Bossin/
2 GIVN Henricus
2 SURN Bossin
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JAN 1863
2 PLAC Kraainem
1 OCCU schaliedekker (roofer)
1 FAMS @F20@
1 FAMC @F16@
1 NOTE A FIFTH CHILD of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]] (2026-07-27), found as a witness
2 CONT at his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding — Kraainem, 25 February 1884 — aged 21,
2 CONT already a *schaliedekker*. That appearance names no parents; it is his own **marriage
2 CONT act**, Kraainem, **23 November 1887** (the act that also brought [[guns_maria_1864]] into the
2 CONT tree), that states them directly: **Guillelmus Bossin**, landbouwer, and **Joanna
2 CONT Catharina Peremans**, landbouwster, both of Kraainem. It also gives his own birth as
2 CONT **Kraainem, 1 January 1863**.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Two identifiers carry the parent link, not one.** First, the parent names on his own
2 CONT 1887 act, matching [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]] exactly. Second, and
2 CONT independent of the first: [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s death — **Kraainem, 10 October 1888** —
2 CONT recurs identically, to the day, in two further acts for two *different* children five
2 CONT years apart: his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s 1901 remarriage and his brother
2 CONT [[bossin_joannes_1866]]'s 1896 Werchter marriage. Two unconnected documents
2 CONT agreeing to the day is what confirms this is the same Guilielmus Bossin family and not a
2 CONT namesake — a real risk in this commune, since [[bossin_joannes_1834]] already turned out to be an
2 CONT entirely different, unconnected Joannes Baptista Bossin two generations earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Age consistency across five appearances (1884–1902) is a DERIVED check, not an
2 CONT independent identifier.** Against the 1 January 1863 birth: 21 at the 1884 wedding
2 CONT (exact), 32 at the 1896 Werchter wedding (one year short of the 33 the date implies), 36
2 CONT at a 1900 Kraainem act (one year short of 37), 38 at his sister's 1901 remarriage (exact),
2 CONT 39 at a 1902 Kraainem act (exact). Two of five a year short is ordinary rounding, the same
2 CONT pattern already accepted on [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s own age record — it shows one continuous man,
2 CONT which the parent-name-plus-death-date pair above had already established; it adds no new
2 CONT identifying weight of its own.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The mother's forename is the already-reconciled variant, not a new dispute.** The 1887
2 CONT act calls her *Joanna Catharina Peremans* — closer to [[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s own anchor act
2 CONT (*Joanna Catharina Jacoba*) than the *Anna Catharina* several other acts in this family
2 CONT use. It applies the standing reconciliation (peremans.md, joannes_bossin51.md,
2 CONT research-log §65) and changes nothing.
2 CONT
2 CONT **UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — BOTH REGISTER IMAGES WERE READ.** His own 1887 Kraainem
2 CONT marriage act confirms his birth directly on the register — **Kraainem, 1 January
2 CONT 1863** — and states his parents were **both present in person and consenting**: *"meerderjarigen
2 CONT zoon van Guillelmus Bossin en van Joanna Catharina Peremans, gehuwden, landbouwers, wonende
2 CONT te Crainhem, beiden alhier tegenwoordig en toestemmende."* That is a hard floor: both
2 CONT parents were demonstrably alive on 23 November 1887, sharpening what
2 CONT [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s own record already treats as his death window. The 1884 Kraainem
2 CONT act (his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding) states the sibship outright as well,
2 CONT independently of this act: *"Henricus Bossin, schaliedekker, oud een en twintig jaren,
2 CONT wonende te Crainhem, **broeder der bruid**"* — no longer resting on the arithmetic
2 CONT coincidence of his stated age alone.
2 CONT
2 CONT **His bride signs a different name from the one the act gives her — recorded, not
2 CONT smoothed over.** [[guns_maria_1864]] is named throughout as *Maria Catharina Guns*, but she signs
2 CONT the register **"Justine Guns"**. A roepnaam (call-name) or a formal/informal name pair used
2 CONT by the same woman for the same act is self-referential and no threat to identity — there is
2 CONT no rival Guns family proposed at Sterrebeek — but it is worth recording exactly as written.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Three brothers-in-law stand witness, two of them frontiers rather than links.**
2 CONT [[swaelens_joannes_1858]], 29, *schrijnwerker*, is stated *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms* — the groom's
2 CONT brother-in-law, and by 1887 resident at **Kraainem** rather than the Alsemberg of his own
2 CONT 1884 wedding, an exact arithmetic match to his 11 May 1858 birth. The other two are new
2 CONT names, and neither act names a wife for either: **Petrus Vanhoudenhoven**, 34 here (30 at
2 CONT the 1884 wedding, so b. ~1853), and **Egidius Franciscus De Hondt**, 26 (b. ~1861), both of
2 CONT Kraainem, both stated *schoonbroeder des bruidegoms*. Each therefore married an
2 CONT unidentified Bossin daughter — see [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] for that frontier, recorded once
2 CONT rather than on every sibling's own page.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: his own civil birth registration (a separate document from this marriage act),
2 CONT and any children of this marriage.
