1 NOTE Father of the groom in his son [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 3, 10
2 CONT April 1900 (S28), which gives his death as **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887**. His son was
2 CONT seven.
2 CONT
2 CONT **RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — not [[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s family.** His own marriage act — Sint-Stevens-
2 CONT Woluwe nr. 4, **17 June 1858** (S33) — was the open question this record carried: whether
2 CONT he descended from the same Bossins as his son's mother-in-law, [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (Antonia
2 CONT Bossin, daughter of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] × [[peremans_joanna_1824]]). It answers no. The act names
2 CONT his own parents as **Judocus Bossin** and **Maria Desmedt**, a dagloonster — a wholly
2 CONT different couple from [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] × [[peremans_joanna_1824]]. Same surname, same commune,
2 CONT two unconnected families a generation apart; that is now settled rather than left as a
2 CONT question. It also supplies his exact birth for the first time — **2 January 1834,
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe** — and his trade there, *daglooner*, and his bride's exact
2 CONT birth, **4 April 1836, Brussel**, where she is recorded as a *verlaten kind* (abandoned
2 CONT child) — see [[wolf_maria_1836]].
2 CONT
2 CONT **Five more children (2026-07-27), all from acts naming this couple as the child's
2 CONT parents:** [[bossin_joannes_1857]] (b. SSW 1857, unmarried on the act — see the flag
2 CONT below), [[bossin_philippus_1859]] (b. SSW 1859), [[bossin_jan_1876]] (b. SSW 1876),
2 CONT [[bossin_frans_1882]] (b. SSW 1882) and [[bossin_guillielmus_1869]] (b. Kraainem 1869, known only
2 CONT from his own 1896 marriage act). [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]] was already the only child this
2 CONT tree held for this couple; these six make seven.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The mother's exact age is the identifier that carries all five.** Against the
2 CONT 1836-04-04 birthdate the 1858 marriage act gives her, her stated age is an *exact* match
2 CONT in five separate acts — 21 (1857), 22 (1859), 39 (1876), 46 (1882) and 43 on
2 CONT [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s own 1879 birth act — five for five, which is what defeats the
2 CONT "two couples" reading the seventeen-year gap between the 1859 and 1876 births might
2 CONT otherwise invite. The father's own age matches exactly in two of those acts and is a year
2 CONT short in two others — ordinary rounding, not a conflict, given the mother's precision on
2 CONT the same documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT **His own death is restated twice more, independently.** [[bossin_jan_1876]]'s 1897
2 CONT marriage act and [[bossin_guillielmus_1869]]'s 1896 marriage act both give his death as
2 CONT **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887** — an exact match, to the day, to what this record
2 CONT already held from S28. Two of his children's own later marriages, nine years apart,
2 CONT independently agree with each other and with the record.
2 CONT
2 CONT **His trade moves with him across seven documents, 1857-1887:** *papiermaekersgast* at 24
2 CONT (1857) → *daglooner* at his own 1858 marriage and again at 25 (1859) → *landbouwer* at 41
2 CONT (1876) and 45 (1879, [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s own birth act) → *herbergier* at 48 (1882),
2 CONT the trade he is still keeping, and the one [[wolf_maria_1836]] continues alone, when he dies in
2 CONT 1887.
2 CONT
2 CONT **FLAG, not resolved — a child born before this marriage.** [[bossin_joannes_1857]] was
2 CONT born **28 June 1857**, about eleven months before this couple's marriage on 17 June 1858.
2 CONT Both dates stand as their own acts give them; neither is altered to make them agree. See
2 CONT his own record for the reasoning, which follows the same shape already documented on
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]].
2 CONT
2 CONT The mother's surname is spelled across these acts as *Dewolf*, *Wolf*, *De Wolf* and *Anna
2 CONT Maria*/*Maria Anna Dewolf* — one woman, several clerks; see [[wolf_maria_1836]].
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: [[bossin_judocus]]'s own marriage and death, neither yet searched for.
