1 NOTE Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 19, 15 Aug 1851**.
2 CONT **Sex is stated in the act** ("Man"), not read off the forename.
2 CONT
2 CONT The father, [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 27, born at
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *daglooner*. The mother, [[peremans_joanna_1824]], is aged 27, born at
2 CONT Zaventem. Both ages fall inside this couple's already-established 1824 birth years, and
2 CONT both birthplaces match exactly — two independent identifiers on each side.
2 CONT
2 CONT A fourth sibling: FamilySearch's index (S24) had already found [[bossin_cornelius_1847]]
2 CONT (1847), [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (1849) and [[bossin_ludovica_1853]] (1853) for this couple, but not this
2 CONT child, born between the second and third of those. This act closes that gap.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A namesake, not a relative — do not confuse with [[bossin_joannes_1834]].** This tree already
2 CONT holds a *different* Joannes Baptista Bossin, husband of [[wolf_maria_1836]] and father of
2 CONT [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]. The two are not the same man and this act does not connect their
2 CONT families: this pass's other finding — [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s own 1858 marriage act — names *his*
2 CONT parents as Judocus Bossin and Maria Desmedt, not [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]].
2 CONT Same forename, same surname, same small commune, two unrelated men a generation apart in
2 CONT the records. See the note on [[bossin_joannes_1834]] for the act that settles this.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The mother's forename here is a reconciled variant, not an open question.** The act
2 CONT calls her *Anna Catharina Peremans*, shorter than this tree's *Joanna Catharina Jacoba*.
2 CONT That is not the unresolved Haesaerts-style conflict flagged elsewhere in this family
2 CONT (§51/§53/§54): the anchor act that put [[peremans_joanna_1824]] in this tree in the first place — her
2 CONT own 1846 marriage act, S19, read as an image — already gives her the full *Joanna
2 CONT Catharina Jacoba Peremans*, and her own record already reasons that shorter forms
2 CONT elsewhere are a clerk's quotation from memory of that document. This 1851 act repeats an
2 CONT already-reconciled shortening; it does not itself have to do the reconciling, which is
2 CONT exactly what distinguishes it from the Haesaerts case, where no document ever settled the
2 CONT variant independently of the disputed act.
2 CONT
2 CONT **CORROBORATED (2026-07-27), independently of his own birth act for the first time.** He
2 CONT stands witness at his sister [[bossin_ludovica_1853]]'s wedding — Kraainem, 25 February 1884 —
2 CONT given as 32, *pleisteraar*. Age 32 on that date is an exact arithmetic match to the
2 CONT 1851-08-15 birth this record already holds.
2 CONT
2 CONT **UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — THE REGISTER IMAGE WAS READ, and it states the
2 CONT relationship outright.** The act's own words, not this tree's inference from a shared
2 CONT birth act: *"Joannes Baptista Bossin, pleisteraar, oud twee en dertig jaren, wonende te
2 CONT Crainhem, **broeder der bruid**"* — brother of the bride, in the register itself. The
2 CONT sibship no longer rests on the arithmetic match to his own 1851 birth act alone.
