1 FAMS @F24@
1 FAMS @F25@
1 FAMC @F16@
1 NOTE Younger sister of [[bossin_antonia_1849]], and one of six known children of [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and
2 CONT [[peremans_joanna_1824]] — a fourth, [[bossin_joannes_1851]] (b. 1851), a fifth, [[bossin_henricus_1863]] (b.
2 CONT 1863), and a sixth, [[bossin_joannes_1866]] (b. 1866), were all found in the same
2 CONT pass that day-dated this birth or the one after it.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Birth dated to the day (2026-07-27), superseding the declaration-date reading.** A
2 CONT separate civil birth act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 18 (S33) — names her directly as the
2 CONT child, states an "hour of birth" of 8:00, and gives its own registration date
2 CONT (*SourceDate*) as the same day, 5 October 1853. Across this corpus, a Geboorte act's
2 CONT EventDate and its SourceDate ordinarily differ by one or two days — a child registered a
2 CONT day or two after the birth — which is what made the earlier FamilySearch declaration date
2 CONT (S24) read as "probably a day late," on the same reasoning already applied to her sister
2 CONT [[bossin_antonia_1849]]'s birth. Here, uniquely, the two dates coincide: an hour is stated, the role is
2 CONT *Kind* rather than a declarant, and there is no registration lag to allow for. That
2 CONT internal evidence — same-day EventDate and SourceDate, plus a stated hour of birth — is
2 CONT why this act is read as giving the birth itself rather than a declaration a day behind it,
2 CONT and the field now carries **1853-10-05** as a day-level date rather than a year with a
2 CONT `raw` declaration note.
2 CONT
2 CONT A FamilySearch declaration index (S24) named her parents as *Guilielmus Bossin* and
2 CONT *Joanna Maria Peremans* against an entry it read as "marriage, 17 February 1884,
2 CONT Alsemberg" — a fourth spelling of her mother's forename, after the *Joanna Catharina
2 CONT Jacoba* of her mother's own act, the *Anna Catharina* of her sister's 1872 act, and the
2 CONT *Anna Catharina* of these birth declarations. **That reading is now known to be the second
2 CONT publication of the marriage banns, not the marriage — see below**; it was S24 correctly
2 CONT transcribing an index row and this record misreading what kind of act the row was.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Her own marriage act, read in full (2026-07-27) — Kraainem, 25 February 1884.** It
2 CONT restates her birth exactly as held here, **5 October 1853, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, and
2 CONT names her parents as **Guillelmus Bossin**, landbouwer, and **Anna Catharina Peremans**,
2 CONT landbouwster, both of Kraainem — a further, independent match to [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]
2 CONT and [[peremans_joanna_1824]], with the mother's forename in the already-reconciled shortened form
2 CONT (see peremans.md, joannes_bossin51.md, research-log §65).
2 CONT
2 CONT **THE REGISTER IMAGE WAS READ (2026-07-27), and the 17-vs-25 February discrepancy is
2 CONT SETTLED.** The Kraainem marriage act states outright that the banns were published "op de
2 CONT Zondagen tienden en zeventienden Februari laatstleden" — Sundays the 10th and 17th of
2 CONT February — at Kraainem and Alsemberg. A second, independent register confirms it: the
2 CONT **Alsemberg banns register itself**, read as an image, carries acts nrs. 7 and 8, each
2 CONT printed **AKTE VAN HUWELIJKSAFKONDIGING**, dated Sunday 10 February ("voor de eerste maal
2 CONT afgekondigd") and Sunday 17 February ("voor de tweede maal afgekondigd") 1884. **S24 was
2 CONT never wrong about the 17th — it correctly read the second banns publication; what was
2 CONT missing was the fact that a banns publication and a marriage are two different acts.**
2 CONT The marriage itself is **25 February 1884, Kraainem**, now the value in this record's
2 CONT frontmatter, matching [[swaelens_joannes_1858]]'s record field for field as the data model requires.
2 CONT The banns dates are kept here, in prose, as what they actually are, not discarded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Confidence is raised to `doc`: both this marriage and the discrepancy that had kept it at
2 CONT `sup` now rest on two independently read register images, not an index row.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The witnesses, all named by relationship in the act's own words.** [[swaelens_franciscus]],
2 CONT 24, is stated *broeder des bruidegoms* — the groom's brother. [[bossin_joannes_1851]], 32, and
2 CONT [[bossin_henricus_1863]], 21, are both stated *broeder der bruid* — her own brothers, no longer
2 CONT resting on inference from their own separate acts alone. **Petrus Vanhoudenhoven**, 30, is
2 CONT stated *schoonbroeder der bruid* — her brother-in-law, meaning a Bossin sister not yet
2 CONT identified in this tree married him; see [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] for that frontier, which a
2 CONT second, independent act in 1887 repeats.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A REMARRIAGE (2026-07-27) — Petrus Vrebos, Kraainem, 30 May 1901.** Not previously in
2 CONT the tree. By then a widow — [[swaelens_joannes_1858]] had died at Kraainem on 7 October 1898, named in
2 CONT this act as her deceased "vorige partner" — she married **[[vrebos_petrus_1856]]**, himself a
2 CONT widower. Her own birth is restated exactly, **5 October 1853, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe**, an
2 CONT exact day-level match confirming this is the same woman. Her father is named **Guillelmus
2 CONT Bossin, dead 10 October 1888, Kraainem** — sharpening [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s held death
2 CONT from a bare year to a day, now corroborated a second time independently by
2 CONT [[bossin_joannes_1866]]'s own 1896 marriage act — and her mother **Anna Catharina
2 CONT Peremans**, the already-reconciled shortened form.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: the 1901 remarriage register image (the 1884 marriage's image is now read), and
2 CONT any children of either marriage.
