1 REFN bossin_ludovicus_1879
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Ludovicus /Bossin/
2 GIVN Ludovicus
2 SURN Bossin
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 DEC 1879
2 PLAC Sint-Stevens-Woluwe
1 OCCU polijster (polisher)
1 FAMS @F23@
1 FAMC @F19@
1 NOTE Married [[thumas_maria_1880]] at Kraainem on **10 April 1900** (act nr. 3, S28). Born at
2 CONT **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 5 December 1879**, a *polijster*, son of [[bossin_joannes_1834]] — dead since
2 CONT 1887 — and [[wolf_maria_1836]], who kept an inn there.
2 CONT
2 CONT **RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — the shared surname is not a shared family.** This record used
2 CONT to leave open whether he shared blood, not just a surname, with his bride's mother
2 CONT [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (Antonia Bossin of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe). His father [[bossin_joannes_1834]]'s own 1858
2 CONT marriage act now names *his* parents — Judocus Bossin and Maria Desmedt — a different
2 CONT couple from Antonia's parents, [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]] and [[peremans_joanna_1824]]. The two Bossin
2 CONT families are not connected by this line. The witnesses at this 1900 wedding — two more
2 CONT Bossins, hoveniers of Zaventem and Kraainem — remain unexplained by this finding; a small
2 CONT commune can still hold more than one unconnected Bossin family, and no claim is made about
2 CONT them here.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Note the id.** He is not [[bossin_ludovica_1853]], Antonia's sister born 1853; the two ids differ
2 CONT by a single letter and the people differ by a generation and a sex. This one carries his birth
2 CONT year for exactly that reason.
2 CONT
