1 NOTE Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 22 Mar 1859**,
2 CONT 03:30. **Sex is stated in the act** ("Man"), not read off the forename.
2 CONT
2 CONT The father, [[bossin_joannes_1834]], self-declares (*aangever*), aged 25, born at
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, a *daglooner* — an exact match to the 1834-01-02 birthdate his own
2 CONT 1858 marriage act gives (his January birthday had passed). The mother, [[wolf_maria_1836]], is
2 CONT aged 22, born at Brussel — an exact match to her own 1836-04-04 birthdate (her April
2 CONT birthday not yet due).
2 CONT
2 CONT **Both parents are marked *ongehuwd* (unmarried) on this act**, despite their marriage at
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 17 June 1858, nine months earlier. This reads as a transcription
2 CONT anomaly rather than a rival couple: every other identifier — both exact ages, both
2 CONT birthplaces, both forenames and surnames — agrees precisely with [[bossin_joannes_1834]] and
2 CONT [[wolf_maria_1836]], and no second couple sharing both names and both birthdates to the year
2 CONT is a plausible alternative. It is recorded rather than smoothed over.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Later seen as a witness.** As *Amandus Bossin*, 48, *landbouwer*, he stands witness at
2 CONT his brother [[bossin_joannes_1857]]'s 1907 wedding — an age consistent with this birth.
2 CONT
