2 CONT both.** The Assenede register has her birth there in 1766; and a *memorie van successie*
2 CONT — an estate-duty declaration, kantoor Hulst nr. 2027 — was filed at Assenede on
2 CONT **27 December 1807** in her name, giving her husband as **[[bouchier_constantin]]**.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three identifiers agree, which is what licences reading the estate as hers: a surname worth
2 CONT 13 bits with an uncommon forename, the death year 1807 that the held record already
2 CONT carried from a different source, and Assenede, where her father was buried in 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The estate date is not a death date.** A memorie is filed after a death, so 27 December
2 CONT 1807 says only that she was dead by then. The year stands as the fact and the filing sits
2 CONT in `raw`, the same distinction [[bundervoet_petrus_1727]]'s burial draws.
2 CONT
