1 NOTE Of Evergem; married twice. His son Segerius (~1615), through whom our line descends,
2 CONT was by his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORRECTED (July 2026), on two points, both against the tree this record already cited.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The surname "Hovelynck" is withdrawn.** This record called Segerius's mother
2 CONT "Elisabeth Hovelynck" and attributed that to the paulderidder tree. That tree records
2 CONT her as "Elisabeth NN" — a given name and nothing else. Where "Hovelynck" came from is
2 CONT not known; it is in no source reachable from here, so it has been removed rather than
2 CONT repeated. She now has her own record as [[elisabeth]], deliberately without a surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The order of the marriages was the wrong way round.** The record had Catharina van
2 CONT Hecke first and Elisabeth second. The children date it the other way: Elisabeth's son
2 CONT Segerius was born about 1615, while Catharina van Hecke (~1620–~1670) is shown in
2 CONT paulderidder under "half-siblings" as the mother of Wilhelmina Bundervoet (~1650).
2 CONT A wife born about 1620 cannot be the earlier marriage of a man whose son arrived in
2 CONT 1615. Elisabeth is therefore first, Catharina second.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both now have records: [[vanhecke_catharina_1620]] and her daughter [[bundervoet_wilhelmina_1650]], along
2 CONT with Segerius's full siblings [[bundervoet_livinus_1615]] and [[bundervoet_maria_1623]]. See also the note on [[vanhecke_willem_1580]]
2 CONT about two van Hecke women marrying into consecutive generations of this family.
