1 FAMS @F35@
1 FAMC @F39@
1 NOTE Younger son of Joannes Bundervoet (~1682–1760) and Livina Stockman, and the brother of
2 CONT Christoffel (1709–1786) through whom our line descends. He existed in this tree only as
2 CONT the string "Pieter (1727)" inside his father's note; every person referenced anywhere is
2 CONT supposed to have their own record, and now he does.
2 CONT
2 CONT The death is recorded as a burial, not a death: paulderidder gives "deceased, aged about
2 CONT 50" with a burial at Assenede on 13 December 1777, and no date of death. The year is
2 CONT safe, the day is the burial's, and the two are kept apart rather than collapsed into a
2 CONT death date the source never gave. Assenede, a little north of Evergem, is also the first
2 CONT sign of this branch moving off the home parish.
2 CONT
2 CONT HIS FAMILY IS NOW IN THE TREE — his wife [[dedeckere_marie_1731]] and all eight children. From
2 CONT paulderidder: married about 1750 to Marie Anna de Deckere (~1731–1809), with Joannis
2 CONT (1751), Livinus (1752), Petronella (1754–1794), Christophorus (1755), Joannis Baptista
2 CONT (1757), Livina Maria (1760–1831), Joanna (1761–1825) and Coleta (1766–1807). They are
2 CONT blood relatives of Renée and Léon — a great-uncle's whole household — and belong in the
2 CONT tree under objective 2. They are listed here rather than grafted because this pass took
2 CONT the direct ancestors first, as the charter's priority requires.
2 CONT
2 CONT A second document sits on his paulderidder profile, captioned "Petrus Bundervoet Akte
2 CONT van teraardebestelling" — a burial act. Not yet retrieved.
2 CONT
2 CONT **NOT PROVEN, refused — the Gent cluster (objective 3, 2026-07-27).** The harvested
2 CONT corpus's own clustering (`coverage.surname_clusters()`) offers this record as the
2 CONT `best_link` for the biggest Gent-city cluster (153 mentions, 131 acts), on the strength of
2 CONT a 30.7-bit, 1-independent-identifier score (name + kin-forename echo) against a "Petrus
2 CONT Bundervoet × Isabella De Coster" whose son Joannes Baptista was born 1836 in Gent. NOT
2 CONT GRAFTABLE, labelled in `research/labels.jsonl`. Two independent grounds refuse it: the
2 CONT spouse named is Livina Quackebeke, not Marie Anna de Deckere; and the chronology is
2 CONT impossible outright — that Petrus fathered sons in ~1790 and 1803, decades after this
2 CONT record's own attested 1777 death (buried Assenede). The Gent surname cluster in fact
2 CONT resolves into **six distinct, unrelated patriarch families** plus a 20th-century line
2 CONT already independently attested — see research-log §73 for the full breakdown. None
2 CONT connects here.
1 SOUR @S44@
2 QUAY 2
