2 SURN Coekelberghs
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1838
2 NOTE Recorded as: alive on 30 October 1838; death not known
1 OCCU landbouwer (farmer)
1 FAMS @F58@
1 NOTE Father of the bridegroom in his son [[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]]'s marriage act — Bertem nr. 8,
2 CONT 30 October 1838, **read as the register image**. A *landbouwer* of Berthem, and the act
2 CONT puts him there in person: *hier present en Consenteerende*. He is not called *wijlen*, so
2 CONT he was alive that day, and he is given no age, so this record carries no birth date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like everyone else named in the act except the witnesses — the bridegroom, the bride and
2 CONT all four parents — he declared he could not sign.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Why this record is `sup` although the image was read.** The image is `doc`-quality
2 CONT evidence for what the 1838 act *says*. It is not evidence that the groom it names is this
2 CONT tree's [[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]]. That bridge runs through the 1873 and 1903 acts, which are
2 CONT AGATHA transcriptions with no scan, so the chain is only as strong as its weakest link.
2 CONT See docs/research-log.md §52 for why that distinction is now enforced, and §53 for this
2 CONT pass.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — his own marriage to [[elseviers_petronella]], which the Bertem registers should
2 CONT hold for roughly 1800–1809 and which would name his parents. The Bertem film that would
2 CONT carry it is **DGS 004471767**, *Geboorten 1796–1870, Huwelijken 1796–1832, Overlijdens
2 CONT 1796–1842* — the three record types are bound as separate blocks rather than interleaved,
2 CONT and there is no index over the film, so it is a browse rather than a lookup.
1 SOUR @S57@
2 QUAY 2
