1 NOTE Named as the child in a civil birth act at **Bertem, 1858-01-15**, which names his father
2 CONT as *Joannes Baptista Coekelberghs* — [[coekelberghs_joannes_1809]], who declared the birth in person,
2 CONT aged 48, born at Bertem — and so places this person in the tree by the act rather than by a
2 CONT name.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act is held in the harvested corpus and reached through Open Archives:
2 CONT https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:a0b8c9a0-322e-f254-e5f4-efcd42d1f8e0
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: an indexed act, not the register image. **No `sex` is recorded**, because the harvested
2 CONT mention carries only the relation role and never a sex, and this project does not read a sex
2 CONT off a forename.
2 CONT
2 CONT RETRACTED IN PART (2026-07-26): **the mother link has been removed.** This record was
2 CONT written with `mother: anna_haesaerts`, but the act does not name her. It names
2 CONT *Anna **Catharina** Haesaerts* — precisely the forename variant that §51 and §53
2 CONT deliberately left **unmerged** with the plain *Anna Haesaerts* of the 1838, 1853, 1873 and
2 CONT 1903 acts. Grafting this child to her would have silently resolved an open question by
2 CONT side effect, which is the way a tree acquires a decision nobody made.
2 CONT
2 CONT The father side is not in doubt: he declares the birth himself, his age and birthplace
2 CONT agree with the 1838 marriage act read in §53, and Bertem is the commune. So the link
2 CONT upward stands and the link across does not.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — one document settles it either way: the **1858 Bertem register image**, or
2 CONT [[haesaerts_anna_1810]]'s own death act, Bertem 8 January 1880. Until one is read, this record
2 CONT has a father and no mother, and that is the honest shape of what is known.
1 SOUR @S56@
