1 NOTE Mother of [[janssen_josephus_1820]], named on his 1851 marriage act (Oostende act nr. 090) as
2 CONT "DECLERCK Victoria, 64, *werkvrouw*" — still living. Her own marriage act, Oostende 17
2 CONT November 1819 (RAB ID 572117), gives her birth as 30/04/1786 at **Klemskerke**, age 33 at
2 CONT the wedding, residence Oostende. The 1820 Oostende birth register, still French at that
2 CONT date, spells her "Declerck Victoire".
2 CONT
2 CONT **A stated conflict, not smoothed over.** A birth of 30/04/1786 makes her 65 at the August
2 CONT 1851 wedding, but that act's Detail transcription gives her age as 64. This is ordinary
2 CONT index slippage on a self-reported age thirty-two years after the fact, and does not veto
2 CONT the identification, which rests on both spouses' exact-matching birth date and place plus
2 CONT a second, independent corroboration of the parent names on [[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s own
2 CONT 1820 birth act.
2 CONT
2 CONT Three further children with [[janssen_joannes_1778]] at Oostende: [[janssen_petrus_1822]]
2 CONT (1822), [[janssen_hermanus_1825]] (1825), [[janssen_clementia_1832]] (1832).
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER, not pursued. Her own parents, per the 1819 act, are **Declerck Pierre × Pauwels
2 CONT Josephe** — both recorded as having died at Klemskerke, no dates given. Rests on that
2 CONT single index row alone, with no independent document. Left unlinked.
