1 NOTE Mother of Marie Catharina Joostens (1810–1857) and so a direct ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named alongside her husband in her daughter's Grez-Doiceau death act of 10 June 1857, which
2 CONT is the only source read for her. It gives her no dates and no place; none is invented here.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surname is Flemish (De Coninck / Deconinck are the commoner spellings) in a
2 CONT Walloon-Brabant setting, which is worth noting for the search: the family may have come to
2 CONT Woluwe-Saint-Lambert or Grez-Doiceau from Flanders, and the name may be spelled either way
2 CONT in the registers.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: the Joostens–Deconninck marriage, and her own parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026): named as the mother of the deceased in her daughter's 1857
2 CONT Grez-Doiceau death act, read at the archive. As with her husband, the act gives her nothing
2 CONT beyond the name.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
