1 REFN dekeyser_rita
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Rita /De Keyser/
2 GIVN Rita
2 SURN De Keyser
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1940 AND 1949
1 FAMC @F91@
1 NOTE Roland's only sister, born in the early-to-mid 1940s — in England if she was born
2 CONT alongside him during the family's wartime years there, in Oostende if before or after.
2 CONT Her birth record is one of the two routes that would confirm Gustaaf × Simonne as a
2 CONT couple, the other being Roland's own 1943 certificate.
2 CONT
2 CONT MERGED (July 2026). This record and a second one, `roland_sis`, described the same
2 CONT person: both were daughters of Gustaaf × Simonne, both were "Roland's sister", both
2 CONT born in the 1940s. `roland_sis` was written when the family could recall a sister but
2 CONT not her name, and this one after the name came out; nothing ever distinguished them.
2 CONT The family knows of one sister, and Gustaaf's record likewise says one daughter. The
2 CONT two are now one, with `roland_sis` deleted rather than left as a second copy.
2 CONT
2 CONT NAME. "Rita" is family recollection, held with some confidence but not documented.
2 CONT
2 CONT SURNAME UNCERTAIN — and deliberately so. Her brother's 1943 Tottenham registration is
2 CONT known to have mangled the Flemish name, and the family does not know how Rita's own
2 CONT was written down. The spelling here is the family's form, not a transcription of any
2 CONT record: treat "De Keyser" as a placeholder until a document settles it. Variants
2 CONT already seen or plausible for an English registrar: Dekeyser, Dekeyster, De Kayser,
2 CONT Keyser. Any index search must run across all of them rather than the Flemish form
2 CONT alone — the wrong spelling is the likeliest reason such a search comes back empty.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: England & Wales GRO birth index, Edmonton registration district (which
2 CONT covered Tottenham) and its neighbours, 1940–1949, mother's maiden name Vandewalle.
2 CONT The mother's-maiden-name field is the strong discriminator — it survives whatever the
2 CONT registrar did to the surname, and it would tie Simonne to this family at the same time.
1 SOUR @S46@
2 QUAY 1
