1 NOTE Born in Tottenham, London in 1943 while his family were WWII refugees (Tottenham was then in the Edmonton registration district); an English registrar mis-wrote the Flemish name. Buried at Stene, Oostende. His 1943 London birth certificate is the key record to confirm his father Gustaaf and mother Simonne Vandewalle — and, if his father died in the war, Simonne likely returned to Oostende a widow with Roland and his sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHECKED, AND THE CORPUS DOES NOT HAVE HIM (July 2026) — the same Josse De Keyser of Aalst,
2 CONT 1809, that the scorer offered for his father. He was born at Tottenham in 1943 and died in
2 CONT 2003, so a Belgian civil-registration corpus was never likely to hold him; the harvest
2 CONT confirms it rather than assuming it.
2 CONT
2 CONT His 1943 birth certificate (England & Wales GRO, Edmonton district) remains the record that
2 CONT would confirm both his parents.
