1 FAMS @F98@
1 NOTE Married [[thumas_georges_1843]] at Grez-Doiceau on **7 October 1868**, which makes her
2 CONT [[thumas_georges_1836]]'s sister-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nothing else is held. The index rows that record the banns and the marriage give her name and
2 CONT no more — no birth, no parents, no trade — so this record has none rather than a guess at any.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED, SECOND INDEX (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-mariages]] independently
2 CONT indexes this marriage, "row 50, 08/10/1868 THUMAS Georges & DERRIDER Sophie" — a second,
2 CONT unrelated compiler agreeing with S25 that it happened, one day off S25's 7 October (the
2 CONT ordinary drift documented across this venue). Its marriage detail pages carry no parents,
2 CONT ages or trade at all, so this can corroborate the event and nothing more.
2 CONT
2 CONT CANDIDATE PARENTS, NOT PROVEN (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] indexes a Sophie
2 CONT Deridder born at Grez-Doiceau on **20 May 1844**, daughter of Isidore Deridder and Cordélie
2 CONT Victorine Lacourt (married there 2 Dec 1839, other children 1840-1853), aged 24 at an
2 CONT October 1868 wedding — agreeing on forename, surname (a spelling variant), commune, and an
2 CONT age consistent with the marriage. Her middle name **Miranda** appears nowhere in this
2 CONT venue. Nothing ties this child to the 1868 groom, and nothing ever could from this venue
2 CONT alone: netradyle's marriage detail pages carry no parents at all, by construction, not
2 CONT merely by omission. Surname + commune is one identifier, and age-consistency is arithmetic
2 CONT that fits any Sophie Deridder of the right cohort. **Isidore Deridder × Cordélie Victorine
2 CONT Lacourt is recorded here as a named frontier only — no father/mother link is made.**
2 CONT
2 CONT VENUE CLOSED (2026-07-27) on the act that would settle it: Open Archives holds zero
2 CONT Huwelijk or Geboorte acts for Grez-Doiceau at all, so `harvest.py` cannot reach the 1868
2 CONT marriage act by any route. FamilySearch (the exact film and image are already known, from
2 CONT S23's own volume) and AGATHA both came back `blocked` this pass — an expired/logged-out
2 CONT session, not a `miss`.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: the marriage act itself, which would give all of it in one page, name her actual
2 CONT parents, and is in the same Grez-Doiceau volume as [[S23]], near image 221.
