2 CONT `data/forenames.json` folds `apollonia~appolonia` and `joanna~johanna`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A second marriage, found without looking for it.** Widowed 26 July 1866, she remarried
2 CONT [[pieren_leopoldus_1839]] at Oostende on 27 October 1868 (act nr. 106, RAB ID 580783), civil
2 CONT status "weduwe". The act's "Previous Partners" table names her first husband exactly —
2 CONT "JANSSEN | Josephus Joannes | Oostende | 26/07/1866" — corroborating
2 CONT [[janssen_josephus_1820]]'s death date and place **from a civil act**, where until now it had
2 CONT rested only on tree-gverdievel. Note for a future search: her 1895 death may be
2 CONT registered under **Pieren**, not Huyghebaert or Janssen.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Her own birth act was not found.** Scope: both spellings (Huyghebaert 2,668 rows,
2 CONT Huygebaert 740), province-wide, all years; Oudenburg 1828–1833 read row by row. Oudenburg
2 CONT 1830 retains only one Huyghebaert row (nr. 96, 26/12/1830) — this reads as an
2 CONT **untranscribed batch, not a contradiction**: her siblings bracket the slot exactly —
2 CONT [[huyghebaert_adelaide_1829]] (04/03/1829, nr. 24) and [[huyghebaert_marie_1832]]
2 CONT (04/03/1832, nr. 20), an 18-month cadence with a gap precisely where 26/09/1830 falls.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nine siblings, all children of [[huyghebaert_hubertus_1791]] × [[derudder_joanna_1793]] at
2 CONT Oudenburg — see his record for the full list.
