1 NOTE Father of [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]], named on her 1851 marriage act (Oostende act nr.
2 CONT 090) as "HUYGHEBAERT Hubertus, *schoenmaker*, living". His own marriage act, Oudenburg 29
2 CONT April 1821, act nr. 24 (RAB ID 253572, microfilm 1358641, remark "SCAN 122 GSU"), gives
2 CONT age 30 (so b. ~1791), *schoenmaker*, residence Oudenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]]'s 1868 remarriage act (Oostende act nr. 106)
2 CONT independently gives his death: **15 March 1857, Oudenburg** — read off the "Decease Date
2 CONT Father" / "Location of Decease Father" fields on the bride's side of the same act already
2 CONT accepted for corroborating her first husband's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ten children with [[derudder_joanna_1793]] at Oudenburg, all sup from the RAB birth index:
2 CONT [[huyghebaert_carolus_1822]] (13/03/1822, apparently died in infancy — see
2 CONT [[huyghebaert_carolus_1823]]), [[huyghebaert_carolus_1823]] (the name reused, 01/02/1823, m.
2 CONT Oudenburg 1846 [[goes_nn]]), [[huyghebaert_augustinus_1824]] (12/05/1824, m. Zandvoorde 1859
2 CONT [[vantyghem_nn]]), [[huyghebaert_adelia_1826]] (13/07/1826), [[huyghebaert_petrus_1827]]
2 CONT (05/08/1827), [[huyghebaert_adelaide_1829]] (04/03/1829), [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]]
2 CONT (26/09/1830 — own birth act not found, see her record), [[huyghebaert_marie_1832]]
2 CONT (04/03/1832), [[huyghebaert_magdalena_1834]] (21/06/1834) and [[huyghebaert_petrus_1837]]
2 CONT (19/02/1837).
2 CONT
2 CONT **FRONTIER, refused despite being right there.** His own parents, per the 1821 act, are
2 CONT **Ferdinandus Huyghebaert × Anna Theresia Termote** — Ferdinandus d. Oudenburg 06/07/1803
2 CONT (17 Messidor XI), Anna Theresia d. Oudenburg 05/05/1804 (15 Floréal XII); both
2 CONT republican-calendar dates convert correctly to their Gregorian equivalents. **Not
2 CONT linked**: this identical name pair recurs as parents in at least four other West-Flemish
2 CONT communes (Eernegem, Leffinge, Westkerke, Oostkerke-bij-Damme) — exactly the
2 CONT surname-and-region trap CLAUDE.md rule 1 exists for, and this single 1821 index row is
2 CONT the only document naming them for *this* family. The document that would settle it: the
2 CONT Detail page of **Oudenburg 1806, RAB 253462** — same name pair as parents, a different
2 CONT child — which could not be pulled this pass. Re-openable there, or at the register image.
