1 FAMS @F82@
1 NOTE Father of Marie Catharina Joostens (1810–1857), who married Georges Thumas — so a direct
2 CONT ancestor through their son Georges Carolus Josephus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named, with his wife, in his daughter's Grez-Doiceau death act of 10 June 1857. That act is
2 CONT the whole of what is known about him here: no dates, no place, no occupation, because it
2 CONT gave none. His daughter's birthplace is recorded there as Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, which is
2 CONT where this couple were most likely living around 1810, but the act does not say so and it
2 CONT is not recorded as a fact about him.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: the Joostens–Deconninck marriage, and his own birth. Woluwe-Saint-Lambert and
2 CONT Grez-Doiceau are the two communes to try, roughly 1800–1810 for the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026): named as the father of the deceased in his daughter's 1857
2 CONT Grez-Doiceau death act, read at the archive. He was added to this tree from an index entry a
2 CONT pass earlier; this is the act behind it. It still gives him no dates, no place and no
2 CONT occupation, so none is recorded.
2 CONT
