2 DATE AFT 1873
2 NOTE Recorded as: alive on 24 April 1873; death not known
1 OCCU landbouwster (farmer)
1 FAMS @F136@
1 NOTE Mother of the groom in her son [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,
2 CONT 24 April 1873. A *landbouwster* of Everberg, present at the wedding and consenting to it,
2 CONT and recorded as unable to write.
2 CONT
2 CONT Everberg is where her son was born, in August 1849, so the family was still there
2 CONT twenty-four years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT **She is a correction, not only an addition.** [[vandenbemden_henricus_1849]]'s record carried, as an
2 CONT unverified Geneanet claim, a mother named *Agatha Langa*. The act names her **Elisabeth
2 CONT Agatha** and spells the surname **Langes**. The forename was incomplete and the surname
2 CONT was wrong; both are now as the act has them, and the Geneanet reading is retired.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date. The death entry records
2 CONT only that she was alive on the day.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: an AGATHA act analysis, not the register image.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — the spelling is worth pinning before it is searched on. *Langes* as written here
2 CONT also occurs as Lange, Langhe and Langens in Brabant registers, and the Geneanet reading
2 CONT *Langa* is a fourth. Her own marriage or her death act at Everberg would settle it, and a
2 CONT surname that rare is one of the few that can be searched on its own.
