1 REFN pardon_franciscus_1830
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Françiscus /Pardon/
2 GIVN Françiscus
2 SURN Pardon
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 FEB 1830
2 PLAC Winksele
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 JUL 1874
2 PLAC Zaventem
1 OCCU dienstbode (servant)
1 FAMS @F15@
1 FAMC @F159@
1 NOTE Married [[bossin_anna_1829]] at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 1 December 1853 (act nr. 9, S22),
2 CONT so he is [[bossin_guilielmus_1824]]'s brother-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at Winksele on 16 February 1830, and living at Zaventem by the time he married,
2 CONT working as a *dienstbode*. He brought his National Militia certificate to the wedding —
2 CONT the act says it was attached to the record — and, like his bride and his parents, declared
2 CONT himself unable to write.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note the spelling: the act writes *Françiscus*, with the cedilla, and that is what this
2 CONT record follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: AGATHA's transcription, not the register image.
2 CONT
2 CONT DIED (2026-07-26): **Zaventem, 18 July 1874**, per three of his children's own later marriage
2 CONT acts — Joanna Coleta's (Zaventem, 29 January 1877), Henricus's (Zaventem, 18 July 1881) and Maria
2 CONT Thérèsia's (Zaventem, 15 November 1886) — each independently naming him as their late father with
2 CONT that exact date and place (`zaventem-pardon-children-marriages-1877-1886`). None of the acts this
2 CONT tree already held for him states a death directly; it comes from his children's own registers,
2 CONT read a generation later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Four children are recorded: [[pardon_henricus_1854]], [[pardon_joanna_1856]], [[pardon_cornelius_1859]]
2 CONT and [[pardon_maria_1863]]. The family's residence moves from Sint-Stevens-Woluwe to Zaventem between
2 CONT the 1856 and 1859 births — one migrating family, not two couples, since the same "Frans Pardon,
2 CONT deceased Zaventem 18/07/1874" and the same mother, Anna Maria Bossin, recur across all three later
2 CONT marriage acts, tying the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe-born and the Zaventem-born children to the same
2 CONT parents. See [[pardon_cornelius_1859]] for the reasoning in full.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — **Isabella Pardon**, stated in her own Zaventem marriage act (to August Deryck, 21 May
2 CONT 1890) to have been born at Zaventem on 16 June 1868, daughter of "Jan Frans Pardon, deceased
2 CONT Zaventem 18/07/1874" and Maria Anna Bossin
2 CONT (https://www.openarchieven.nl/abl:d81c47c5-c5c5-a339-0df1-03d43a09b42c). Both the father's death
2 CONT date and place and the mother's name match this couple exactly, and her stated birth year would
2 CONT make her a fifth child, younger than [[pardon_maria_1863]]. No birth act naming her has turned up in
2 CONT the held corpus — the date above is what her own marriage act states about her, not a birth
2 CONT registration — so she stays a named frontier and not a record of her own.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — the Winksele births of February 1830 and his parents' own marriage, which would
2 CONT carry [[pardon_guilielmus]] and [[pergijsels_maria]] back a generation.
