1 NOTE A fifth sibling for [[peremans_joanna_1824]]. He married **Joanna Catharina Van Gindertaelen** at
2 CONT **Zaventem on 21 August 1848** (S34), banns published on 6 and 13 August. He was **28**,
2 CONT an *arbeider*, and the act states he could not write and had already completed his
2 CONT militia obligations; she was **23**, an *arbeidster*, also unable to write. Twenty-eight
2 CONT in August 1848 gives the *about 1820* birth year here — an age converted to a year and
2 CONT marked approximate, not a date the act itself gives.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Two independent identifiers anchor the parent link**, not one. First: the act names his
2 CONT mother as *Joanna Theresia Peremans* — read [[verelst_joanna]] — already dead, at
2 CONT **Zaventem, 19 December 1843**, an exact day-level match to the death date this tree
2 CONT already holds for her, drawn from a *separately transcribed* Demogen batch (S19, his
2 CONT sister's 1846 marriage act, a different register entirely). Second: his father is named
2 CONT as *Egidius Peremans*, matching [[peremans_egidius]] by name and commune. A day-level
2 CONT death date repeated identically across two independent transcriptions of two different
2 CONT registers is not the kind of thing two unrelated Egidius Peremans × Joanna Theresia
2 CONT Verelst couples would coincidentally share.
2 CONT
2 CONT **This clears a higher bar than the three siblings already in the tree.**
2 CONT [[peremans_cornelius]], [[peremans_joannes_1822]] and [[peremans_maria]] were each
2 CONT grafted on the parent-name pair alone, with the commune supplied only by the title of the
2 CONT volume the indexed page sat in, and with no exact date anywhere in the record. This act
2 CONT gives an exact day-level date on one of the two parents, independently corroborating a
2 CONT fact already held rather than merely repeating an unanchored name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents are named directly in the act, with their roles labelled, so there is no
2 CONT identity question to resolve: **Joannes Franciscus Van Gindertaelen** (present and
2 CONT consenting) × **Anna Catharina Huenaerts** (present and consenting), both *arbeider(ster)*
2 CONT of Zaventem — see [[vangindertaelen_joannes]] and [[huenaerts_anna]].
2 CONT
2 CONT **Four witnesses stood at the wedding.** Two are already-held siblings and add little:
2 CONT [[peremans_cornelius]], 33 (implying a birth around 1814–1815, recorded on his own record
2 CONT as a witness-line lead, not a date), and [[peremans_joannes_1822]], 26 (consistent with
2 CONT his already-held ~1822, adding no precision). A third, **Petrus Van Der Varen**, 35, is a
2 CONT plausible but unconfirmed match for [[peremans_maria]]'s husband
2 CONT [[vandervarent_petrus_1813]] — the surname is spelled differently here, the act states no relation,
2 CONT and the reasoning is recorded on his own record as a frontier, not a link. The fourth,
2 CONT **Franciscus Engels**, 38, *veldwachter* (rural constable), is not a family lead at all: he
2 CONT is a recurring professional witness, not kin — see the note on that below.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A conflict, not smoothed over.** This act gives Egidius Peremans's own death as
2 CONT **1836-03-06** — one year off the **1837-03-06** already held from S19. Both dates and
2 CONT the reasoning for leaving the question open are recorded on [[peremans_egidius]] itself,
2 CONT not resolved here.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A recurring non-candidate.** *Franciscus Engels, veldwachter*, also witnesses
2 CONT [[peremans_joanna_1824]]'s own 1846 marriage act at Zaventem, aged 35 there and 38 here — the two ages
2 CONT intersect cleanly at a birth in Feb–Aug 1810, consistent with one man holding a single
2 CONT per-commune post across both weddings. No person file is warranted for a recurring
2 CONT professional witness.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — his own birth act at Zaventem around 1820, and any children of this marriage.
2 CONT No search has been made for a rival Egidius Peremans × Joanna Theresia Verelst couple
2 CONT elsewhere in Vlaams-Brabant: the identical day-level death date made it seem unnecessary,
2 CONT but that is a judgement, not a search, and it is recorded here as unchecked rather than
2 CONT as checked.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: an index-level AGATHA/Demogen act analysis, no register image read. A FamilySearch
2 CONT scan exists (`ark:/61903/3:1:S3HY-6423-8F1?i=24`) but is behind a login wall — confirmed
2 CONT `blocked` this pass, a one-request retry, not yet a scoped miss.
