1 FAMS @F1@
1 NOTE Named as father of the groom in his son [[swaelens_joannes_1858]]'s marriage act — Kraainem, 25
2 CONT February 1884 — resident **Braine-l'Alleud**, *hovenier*. The act gives him no age and no
2 CONT dates, so this record has none.
2 CONT
2 CONT **UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27) — no longer single-source.** The Kraainem act's own
2 CONT register image was read: he was **present in person and consenting**, and the act states
2 CONT he **could not sign, being illiterate** ("verklaart niet te kunnen teekenen, ongeletterd
2 CONT zijnde"), a detail only the image carries. A second, independent register corroborates
2 CONT him before the act existed at all — the **Alsemberg marriage banns**, nrs. 7 and 8 (10 and
2 CONT 17 February 1884), a different commune, a different register series and a different
2 CONT clerk, name the same pair: *Egidius Swaelens, hovenier, wonende te Braken-Eigen
2 CONT [Eigenbrakel = Braine-l'Alleud]*. Two independent identifiers — occupation (*hovenier*)
2 CONT and residence (Braine-l'Alleud) — now agree across two unconnected registers, which is
2 CONT what lifts this record off the single-act standard it was accepted at (see
2 CONT [[bossin_cornelius_1847]], [[bossin_joannes_1851]] and [[bossin_antonia_1849]] (Antonia) for that standard).
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: his marriage to [[ackermans_joanna]], and his own birth and death.
1 SOUR @S1@
