1 REFN swaelens_franciscus
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Franciscus /Swaelens/
2 GIVN Franciscus
2 SURN Swaelens
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1859 AND 1860
1 OCCU schrijnwerker (carpenter)
1 FAMC @F1@
1 NOTE **A REFUSAL ANSWERED BY THE DOCUMENT (2026-07-27).** He stands witness at his brother
2 CONT [[swaelens_joannes_1858]]'s wedding — Kraainem, 25 February 1884 — aged 24, resident
2 CONT **Sint-Genesius-Rode**, a *schrijnwerker*, the groom's own trade. Research-log §72 found
2 CONT him in the same act and explicitly refused to graft him as a relative: a shared surname
2 CONT plus a shared trade is one correlated signal, not the two independent identifiers Rule 1
2 CONT requires, since a trade runs in families and apprenticeships. **The register image, read
2 CONT this pass, states the relationship outright and removes the need to infer it**: *"Franciscus
2 CONT Swaelens, schrijnwerker, oud vier en twintig jaren, wonende te Sint-Genesius Rhode,
2 CONT **broeder des bruidegoms**"* — brother of the groom, in the act's own words. He also
2 CONT signs the register himself ("Fs Swaelens").
2 CONT
2 CONT That makes him a son of [[swaelens_egidius]] and [[ackermans_joanna]], alongside
2 CONT [[swaelens_joannes_1858]]. No birth date is stated on the act — only his age, 24, on 25 February 1884 —
2 CONT so this record holds the year span that age permits, **1859..1860**, and no point year.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The methodological point, not just the outcome.** §72's refusal was the right call on
2 CONT the evidence then in hand: no act named a relationship, and the surname-plus-trade
2 CONT correlation is exactly the kind of single, non-independent signal Rule 1 exists to keep
2 CONT out of the tree. It was overturned by reading the primary document itself, not by a better
2 CONT score or a change of mind — the loop working as designed, in both directions.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: his own birth and marriage, and whether he too settled in Kraainem or stayed at
2 CONT Sint-Genesius-Rode.
1 SOUR @S115@
