1 FAMS @F148@
1 FAMC @F137@
1 NOTE The first of FOUR consecutive carpenter (menuisier) generations of Thumas in Grez-Doiceau. Recorded as a godfather (1771) and marriage witness (1775).
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED (July 2026) by his own death act — Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808, the date
2 CONT this record already held, to the day. The act names his father as Lambert Thumas, his
2 CONT mother as Marie Leclercq and his wife as Marie Catherine Noël, so it confirms three links
2 CONT at once: [[thumas_jean_1701]], [[leclercq_marie_1710]] and the marriage to [[noel_marie_1751]], all of which
2 CONT stood on the m2155 tree alone until now.
2 CONT
2 CONT A NEAR-MISS WORTH KEEPING. Before the Thumas harvest was complete, the corpus offered a
2 CONT different man for this record and scored him STRONG: *Martin Joseph* Thumas, who died at
2 CONT Grez-Doiceau on 15 February 1808 — same surname, same parish, same year, three agreeing
2 CONT identifiers. He was rejected because the given names are different men and the days do
2 CONT not match, and that rejection was right; the true act only appeared once more of the
2 CONT surname had been harvested. The lesson is the one the charter states: surname plus place
2 CONT plus year is three agreements and still not an identification.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026). His own death act — Grez-Doiceau, akte nr. 58, registered 21 November
2 CONT 1808 and stating the death as the **20th** — has been read at the archive and saved
2 CONT ([[george-thumas-1808-death-grez-doiceau]]). It confirms the death date exactly, gives his
2 CONT trade as *menuisier*, the word this record already carried, and names his father, mother and
2 CONT wife: [[thumas_jean_1701]], [[leclercq_marie_1710]] and [[noel_marie_1751]]. Three links off a member tree and
2 CONT onto a civil act.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A conflict, left open.** The act says he was **60**, which puts his birth around 1747–48;
2 CONT this record says **14 March 1744**, which would make him 64. The birth date is unchanged,
2 CONT because an age in a death act is hearsay — reported here by a 32-year-old day-labourer — and
2 CONT routinely a few years out, while a stated date is at least a claim about a particular record.
2 CONT Neither is documented. The Grez-Doiceau baptisms for 1744 and 1747–48 would settle it.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE AGE CONFLICT IS NOT SETTLED BY FAMILYSEARCH — and the reason matters. Its index of this
2 CONT family gives his birth as **1748**, which looks at first like independent support for the
2 CONT 1808 act's "age 60" against this record's 1744. It is not independent: FamilySearch is
2 CONT indexing *that same act*, and 1748 is simply 1808 minus 60. Two sources agreeing are not two
2 CONT sources when one is computed from the other.
2 CONT
2 CONT What does bear on it is the family's own shape. His parents married at Wavre on
2 CONT **23 February 1743**, and FamilySearch holds a sister, **Catherine Josephe Thumas**, born
2 CONT **1745** to the same Lambert Thumas × Marie Leclercq and buried at Grez-Doiceau on 22 February
2 CONT 1823. A first son in March 1744, thirteen months after the wedding, then a daughter in 1745,
2 CONT is an ordinary sequence. A first son in 1748, five years after the wedding and three years
2 CONT after his sister, is less ordinary. That leans towards the 1744 this record already holds,
2 CONT without proving it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Still unresolved, and the record that would resolve it is his baptism: Grez-Doiceau parish
2 CONT register, 1744 and 1747–48. Not indexed by name in either archive, so it needs the register
2 CONT images read page by page — or FamilySearch's full-text search over them.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
