1 FAMS @F166@
1 FAMC @F148@
1 NOTE Second of the four carpenter generations; had ten children and lived to age 90.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026) — the corpus's best match for this record is not him.
2 CONT It offers *Lambert Thumas*, who died at **Brussels on 28 February 1801**, and scores it 46
2 CONT bits on surname, place of origin (Grez-Doiceau), a mother and a spouse. Ours died at
2 CONT Grez-Doiceau in **1863**, sixty-two years later.
2 CONT
2 CONT What produced the score is worth naming, because it will recur: the agreement on "mother"
2 CONT and "spouse" is on FORENAMES only. That man's mother was Marie Joseph **Docq** and his wife
2 CONT Marie Catherine **Becquevort**; ours are Marie Catherine **Noël** and Marie Anne Catherine
2 CONT **Quinart**. Two women called Marie Catherine in one Walloon village is no evidence at all,
2 CONT and the surnames — the part that would have been evidence — disagree outright.
2 CONT
2 CONT A high score with a dead man's date sixty years out is the shape of a coincidence, not a
2 CONT find. Left ungrafted and uncited.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26): named, with [[quinart_marie_1780]], as a parent of the deceased in his son
2 CONT [[thumas_georges_1804]]'s death-act extract (S23) — *fils de Lambert Georges Thumas et de Marie
2 CONT Catherine Quinart, **décédés***.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the **first documentary evidence for this record at all**; it had rested entirely on
2 CONT Geneanet. It does not give his dates, but it does place him: he was dead by 28 September
2 CONT 1868, which is consistent with the 1863 death held here, and it puts his fatherhood of
2 CONT Georges on an act of civil registration rather than on a tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note the name order. This record and Geneanet call him *Georges Lambert*; the extract writes
2 CONT *Lambert Georges*, and AGATHA's Grez-Doiceau acts write him both ways and sometimes simply
2 CONT *Lambert*. The forms are recorded as variants, not resolved — his own acts would settle it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Confidence stays `sup`: nothing here documents his own birth, marriage or death, only that he
2 CONT was his son's father and dead by 1868.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED, INDEX-LEVEL (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently
2 CONT indexes his birth as **17 February 1772** at Grez — matching this record's day-level date
2 CONT exactly, with none of the 1-2 day drift seen elsewhere in this venue — naming his own
2 CONT parents as Georges Thumas and Marie Catherine Noël, and their marriage as 3 January 1771,
2 CONT nine months before. This is the first evidence for this generation from a source other
2 CONT than Geneanet.
2 CONT
2 CONT CONFLICT, RECORDED NOT RESOLVED (2026-07-27): the same venue indexes his own marriage to
2 CONT [[quinart_marie_1780]] as **2 April 1799**, two years before the 9 February 1801 this record carries
2 CONT from Geneanet — a two-year gap, not the 1-2 day slippage seen on birth dates elsewhere in
2 CONT this pass. Neither figure is a register image; this is one unauthenticated 2006 index
2 CONT against one member tree, and nothing here decides between them. It narrows, without
2 CONT closing, the argument [[thumas_georges_1804]]'s own §49 note makes about his birth year — see that
2 CONT record.
