1 NOTE The migration generation: born in the Thumas heartland of Grez-Doiceau, he broke the four-generation carpentry tradition to become a farmer and innkeeper, moving north to Kraainem and then Sint-Stevens-Woluwe — founding the Kraainem Thumas family. Widowed of Antoina Bossin (d. 1894), he later partnered Maria Dehoux.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOCUMENTED (July 2026) as the bridegroom's father in the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), living at Kraainem, with
2 CONT his trade given as *landbouwer en herbergier* — exactly the occupation this record already
2 CONT carried, which is itself a check that this is the same man. The act fixes him as the
2 CONT father of [[thumas_joannes_1876]] and the husband of [[bossin_antonia_1849]].
2 CONT
2 CONT His own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872, naming his parents as Georges Thumas and
2 CONT Maria Catharina Joostens — is held in the harvested corpus and not yet read on AGATHA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ALSO DOCUMENTED (July 2026) by his own marriage act — Kraainem, 20 June 1872 — the one
2 CONT this record's `detail` already dated. It names him as the bridegroom, born at Grez-Doiceau,
2 CONT son of **Georges Thumas** and **Maria Catharina Joostens**, so it proves the links to
2 CONT [[thumas_georges_1804]] and [[joostens_marie_1810]] as well as the marriage to [[bossin_antonia_1849]].
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (July 2026). His own 1872 marriage act gives his birth as 15 September 1836 at
2 CONT Grez-Doiceau — as held — and his trade then as *fabrieksgast*, a factory hand. Thirty years
2 CONT later, in his son's 1902 act, he is a *landbouwer en herbergier*. One man, two stages of a
2 CONT life; the occupation field keeps the later one because that is how the family is remembered,
2 CONT and this note keeps the earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER CLOSED, AND THEN SOME (2026-07-26). The 1899 Kraainem act naming Henrica was opened,
2 CONT and searching the surname pair *Thumas Bossin* found two more like it. **Three daughters, all
2 CONT from acts naming this couple as the bride's parents:**
2 CONT
2 CONT - [[thumas_joanna_1873]], b. Kraainem 21 March 1873, m. Jan Baptist Coppens there 27 July 1892 (S26)
2 CONT - [[thumas_henrica_1878]], b. Kraainem 24 June 1878, m. Franciscus Coenraets there 15 April 1899 (S27)
2 CONT - [[thumas_maria_1880]], b. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe 18 August 1880, m. Ludovicus Bossin there 10 April 1900 (S28)
2 CONT
2 CONT With [[thumas_joannes_1876]], who married at Kraainem in 1902, that is four children — and the acts
2 CONT track his own life alongside them. He is a *fabriekbediende* in 1892 and a *herbergier* by
2 CONT 1899, which is the move into the inn this record already described. The 1892 act has
2 CONT [[bossin_antonia_1849]] alive and keeping house; the 1899 and 1900 acts give her death date exactly.
2 CONT
2 CONT STILL OPEN — **a fifth child, probably a son.** A witness at the 1900 wedding is *Georgius
2 CONT Thumas, 24, of Kraainem, fabriekwerker*, and a *Georgius Thumas* witnesses at the 1902 wedding
2 CONT too. Born about 1875–76, in this couple's commune, standing at two of their children's
2 CONT weddings. He is almost certainly their son and he is **not grafted**, because a witness entry
2 CONT gives no parents and this family has already produced two brothers called Georges one
2 CONT generation up.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR SIBLINGS (2026-07-26), from FamilySearch's index of the Grez-Doiceau civil registers
2 CONT (S25), searched by both parents at once: [[thumas_marie_1835]] declared 11 August 1835,
2 CONT [[thumas_georges_1843]] 31 March 1843, [[thumas_jean_1845]] 20 August 1845, and [[thumas_charles_1850]], born
2 CONT 1850 and dead at Grez-Doiceau on 9 April 1851.
2 CONT
2 CONT **His own record is what makes them safe.** His declaration sits in the same series on 16
2 CONT September 1836, one day after the 15 September 1836 birth read from his 1872 act at the
2 CONT archive. A child already documented, inside the sequence, with the same parents and commune,
2 CONT is worth more than any name-matching at the edges of it.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A warning for every later pass: he had a brother also called Georges.** He is *Georges
2 CONT Charles Joseph*, born 1836, married at Kraainem in 1872. [[thumas_georges_1843]] is *Georges
2 CONT Joseph*, born 1843, married at Grez-Doiceau in 1868. Same parents, same surname, both
2 CONT "Georges Thumas" to a careless index. They are not to be merged.
2 CONT
2 CONT DOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, in the sweep of docs/research-log.md §52.
2 CONT Nothing here was refuted and no fact changed. What changed is the honest name for the
2 CONT evidence: every act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis — the Rijksarchief's own
2 CONT Demogen transcription — and AGATHA holds no scan for any of them. `doc` means an act or
2 CONT its image was actually read. None was. The register images are the named next step.
2 CONT
2 CONT FORENAME LEFT OPEN, NOT MERGED (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-naissances]] independently
2 CONT indexes a birth on his exact date with his exact parents — 15 September 1836, father
2 CONT Georges, mother `JOUSTEN Marie Catherine` — but the child is entered as **THUMAS Grégoire
2 CONT Charles Joseph**, not Georges Charles Joseph. The identity is accepted: same event, same
2 CONT parents, no rival birth indexed at Grez in 1836, and his own 1872 Kraainem marriage act —
2 CONT read as an IMAGE — already gives *Georges Carolus Josephus* with these same parents. The
2 CONT forename itself is NOT PROVEN: two index-level sources disagree and neither is an image,
2 CONT and `data/forenames.json` folds no Georges/Grégoire pair — checked directly, and correctly
2 CONT kept apart, since Grégoire is independently attested in this same family (Lambert Grégoire
2 CONT in the 1799 marriage index above; a Grégoire Joseph born 1812) and so is not an implausible
2 CONT reading in its own right. Following the §54 precedent: the recorded forename stands as it
2 CONT is, and this is named as a frontier, not decided.
