1 NOTE Younger brother of [[thumas_georges_1836]], and **the reason his father's death act survives at
2 CONT all**. He married **Sophie Miranda Deridder** at Grez-Doiceau on **7 October 1868**, with
2 CONT banns on 20 and 27 September. Because his father was dead, the commune drew up an extract of
2 CONT [[thumas_georges_1804]]'s 1864 death act on **28 September 1868** and bound it into the marriage
2 CONT volume — that extract is [[S23]], the document that finally put his father's death date and
2 CONT his grandparents' names onto civil registration. This wedding is why it exists.
2 CONT
2 CONT His own birth was declared at Grez-Doiceau on **31 March 1843**; the birth itself is a day or
2 CONT two earlier, which is why it sits in `raw`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Do not merge him with his brother.** [[thumas_georges_1836]] is *Georges Charles Joseph*, born 1836,
2 CONT married at Kraainem in 1872. This is *Georges Joseph*, born 1843, married at Grez-Doiceau in
2 CONT 1868. Two sons of one couple, both called Georges, seven years apart — exactly the confusion
2 CONT this project's rules exist to catch.
2 CONT
2 CONT `sup`: index rows only, no register image read.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: the 1868 marriage act, which would give his trade, his exact birth and his wife's
2 CONT parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED, SECOND INDEX (2026-07-27): [[netradyle-grez-mariages]] independently indexes
2 CONT the marriage — "row 50, 08/10/1868 THUMAS Georges & DERRIDER Sophie" — a second, unrelated
2 CONT compiler agreeing with S25 that this wedding happened at Grez-Doiceau in October 1868. Its
2 CONT date, 8 October, is one day off the 7 October held here from S25; ordinary drift, not a
2 CONT conflict, and this venue's marriage detail pages carry no parents, ages or trade in any
2 CONT case, so this can only corroborate the event, never supply what the FRONTIER above is
2 CONT still asking for.
2 CONT
2 CONT VENUE CLOSED (2026-07-27): the target act was checked against the local corpus directly.
2 CONT Open Archives holds **zero** Huwelijk or Geboorte acts for Grez-Doiceau at all — every one
2 CONT of its mentions there is an Overlijden — so neither the commune's own index nor
2 CONT `harvest.py` can reach this marriage by any route; a bulk or targeted pull would be
2 CONT wasted. FamilySearch (the exact film and image are already known, from S23's own volume)
2 CONT and AGATHA both came back `blocked` this pass — an expired/logged-out session, not a
2 CONT `miss` — so this remains the single highest-value open target on the Thumas line, waiting
2 CONT on a session rather than on more searching.
2 CONT
2 CONT NEGATIVE, SCOPED (2026-07-27): his own birth is absent from
2 CONT [[netradyle-grez-naissances]]'s Thumas-surname Grez-Doiceau births table — 134 rows,
2 CONT fully paged, no `&pg=2` truncation trap — while four of his siblings appear in the same
2 CONT table (Marie Thérèse Stéphanie 1835, the 1836 child, Jean Baptiste Zénon 1845, Charles
2 CONT Eugène 1850). The only 1843 row at all is Rosalie Céline, 14 May. Read as a coverage gap
2 CONT in one 2006 volunteer dépouillement, not evidence of a birth elsewhere: his existence and
2 CONT 1868 marriage already rest on S23 (a register **image**) and S25 (FamilySearch's
2 CONT independent index).
