1 REFN vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Antoine Joseph Albert /Vanalderweireldt/
2 GIVN Antoine Joseph Albert
2 SURN Vanalderweireldt
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 MAY 1780
2 PLAC Diksmuide
1 DEAT
2 DATE JUL 1808
2 PLAC Diksmuide
1 OCCU werkman (labourer)
1 FAMS @F194@
1 NOTE Died young, at 28, only months after the birth of his son Carolus.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE MARRIAGE ACT REACHED (2026-07-27) — Diksmuide, 8 June 1803 (19 Prairial XI, the
2 CONT Republican-calendar conversion checked by computation), act nr. 14, RAB ID 84989
2 CONT (`data/artifacts/vanalderweireldt-wyllie-1803-marriage-diksmuide.md`). The act image itself
2 CONT is FamilySearch film 1166236, image 962, ark `3:1:33SQ-GGKY-9C7D` — 403 unauthenticated, a
2 CONT one-request retry once a session exists — so everything here is a volunteer INDEX/Detail
2 CONT transcription, `sup` throughout, never `doc`. It gives his birth as 09/05/1780, matching
2 CONT this record exactly (the first identifier), age 23, *werkman*, and names both his own
2 CONT parents and [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]]'s in the same document. **His own death act** — Diksmuide,
2 CONT act nr. 97, RAB ID 2299984 — independently gives his age as 28 and birthplace Diksmuide,
2 CONT consistent with the same birth date: the second identifier. No rival Vanalderweireldt
2 CONT couple was found in the area (a Bernard Carol Vanalderweireldt × Regina Papegay, d. 1820,
2 CONT is a different family, checked and set aside).
2 CONT
2 CONT THE DEATH DAY RETRACTED (2026-07-27). This record held 21 July 1808 as a day-level death
2 CONT date. That value is the death act's **Certificate Date** column — the day the death was
2 CONT *registered* — not a stated day of death; the act's own Date column is blank. No two of the
2 CONT three transcriptions that give a day for his death agree with each other: **6 July 1808**
2 CONT (his widow's 1818 remarriage act, Previous-Partners table —
2 CONT `data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`), **16 July 1808** (his son
2 CONT [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]]'s 1828 marriage act) and **21 July 1808** (the certificate date, this
2 CONT death act — `data/artifacts/vanalderweireldt-antoine-1808-death-diksmuide.md`). July 1808 is
2 CONT solid across all three; the day is not, so the day-level precision is withdrawn and only the
2 CONT month is held. What would settle it: the death act's own register image (FamilySearch film
2 CONT 4794755, 403 unauthenticated) or either son's 1828 marriage act image.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR PARENTS NAMED, NONE GRAFTED. The 1803 act names his parents **Vanaldeweireldt Jacques
2 CONT Ignace × Verhaeghe Isabella Claire**, both said to have been born at Langemark (his mother
2 CONT at Diksmuide). The document was reached and read; the generation above it is still a
2 CONT frontier, not a link — the same standard this pass applied throughout. The mother, Isabella
2 CONT Claire/Clara Verhaeghe, leans toward acceptance: named identically across **three**
2 CONT independent acts (this one, his own 1808 death act, and the 1857 death act of a probable
2 CONT sister below), with no rival family found. The father does not clear the same bar: he is
2 CONT **Jacques Ignace** here, **François** on the 1808 death act, and **Jacobus Ignatius** on the
2 CONT 1857 act — the same man beyond real doubt, but no two of the three readings of his forename
2 CONT agree. No father/mother is set on this record.
2 CONT
2 CONT A PROBABLE ELDER SISTER, NOT GRAFTED. **Maria Joanna Vanalderweireldt**, died Diksmuide act
2 CONT 211, certificate 30 September 1857, aged 82y 8m 28d, born Diksmuide, father Jacobus
2 CONT Ignatius, mother Isabella Clara Verhaeghe — a third act naming that parent pair. Working
2 CONT back from the certificate date, 82y 8m 28d before 30 September 1857 lands on 2 January 1775
2 CONT almost exactly (checked by computation) — about 5.3 years before this record's own birth, a
2 CONT plausible elder sister. But she cannot be linked as a sibling while the parents themselves
2 CONT are only a frontier, and her own date is back-computed from a certificate date, carrying the
2 CONT same registration lag documented above — so this stays "about 1775-01-02", a named frontier
2 CONT in prose, not a person file.
2 CONT
2 CONT TWO MORE SONS FOUND WITH [[vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808]] (2026-07-27). [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]], born **three
2 CONT days** after this couple's own wedding — 11 June 1803 (22 Prairial XI) against the 8 June
2 CONT wedding, checked by computation both ways and read as the ordinary "married to legitimate a
2 CONT child already due" pattern rather than a transcription slip; and [[vanalderweireldt_jean]], who died
2 CONT in infancy in January 1805. Full detail, spouse and sources on each of their own records.
2 CONT
2 CONT TWO FRONTIERS SCOPED AND LEFT OPEN. No death act for **Jacobus Ignatius Vanalderweireldt**
2 CONT or **Isabella Clara Verhaeghe** was found in the Diksmuide death index under any spelling
2 CONT tried — they most plausibly died before civil registration began, i.e. they sit in the
2 CONT parish registers. And the Diksmuide **birth** index for 1796–1815 is a blind window of
2 CONT exactly the same shape already documented for the Vincke family a generation later: it
2 CONT carries a bare father surname, no forename and no mother at all, so this generation's
2 CONT sibship cannot be fixed from the birth side — only from the marriage and death acts above.
1 SOUR @S126@
