2 CONT HIS OWN 1828 MARRIAGE ACT RESTATES HIS PARENTS (2026-07-27) — Diksmuide, 4 June 1828, act
2 CONT nr. 106, RAB ID 85449, microfilm 1166239 (VANALDEWEIRELDT Carolus Ludovicus × DUTREEUW
2 CONT Eugenia Henrica, son of VANALDEWEIRELDT Antonius × WYLLIE Brigitta) — a second, independent
2 CONT civil act on the same parent pair, 25 years after [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] and [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]]'s
2 CONT own wedding. It also gives both parents' death dates: father 21 July 1808 (the Certificate
2 CONT Date column of his death act, now understood to be a registration date rather than the day
2 CONT itself — see [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]) and mother 8 November 1824 (matching this couple's held
2 CONT value for [[wyllie_brigitte_1779]] to the day). SPELLING TRAP: this act writes the surname
2 CONT VANALDEWEIRELDT — no R after -ALD- — so it is invisible to a `naam=Vanalderweireldt` query
2 CONT and surfaced only via the mother's surname Wyllie and the bride's surname Dutreeuw.
2 CONT
2 CONT HIS OWN BIRTH REGISTRATION CORROBORATES THE HELD DATE (2026-07-27). The Diksmuide birth
2 CONT index carries a bare row "VANALDERWEIRELDT Charles, certificate 12/03/1808" with no parents
2 CONT attached — part of the same 1796–1815 blind window noted on [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]'s record, so
2 CONT it cannot by itself prove the link — but its certificate date sits one day after this
2 CONT record's held birth of 11 March 1808, the ordinary declaration lag, and the 1828 marriage
2 CONT act above independently states the same 11 March 1808. Two acts agree; the held date is
2 CONT unchanged.
