1 FAMS @F195@
1 FAMC @F113@
1 NOTE Daughter of Carolus Vanalderweireldt & Eugenia Dutreeuw; mother of Emma Celesta Vincke
2 CONT (1880–1974), and of at least seven more children.
2 CONT
2 CONT **NAMED AS MOTHER IN A REGISTER IMAGE FOR THE FIRST TIME (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.**
2 CONT [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s own birth act, read as the register image itself
2 CONT ([[fs-diksmuide-civil-registers-film-004833210]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-act-image.md`), names her mother and gives, **for
2 CONT the first time anywhere in this tree**, her occupation: ***kantwerkster*** (lacemaker).
2 CONT Her surname was re-cropped at 6× zoom in three passes to settle a prior "not
2 CONT letter-by-letter certain" caveat: the **R after `-ALD-`** is clearly present — ruling out
2 CONT the `VANDERWEIRELT` no-R variant that hid records elsewhere in this family — and the
2 CONT final cluster reads **`-eldt`**, tighter than the artifact's own original reading. Her
2 CONT stated age, "vyf en dertig" (35), is one year above the 34y2m she would have completed
2 CONT against this record's held birth of 23 November 1845 — **not treated as a contradiction**:
2 CONT the identical +1 offset recurs independently on her alone in a wholly separate 1888
2 CONT document, her son [[vincke_alfons_1865]]'s marriage act (43 stated vs 42 completed) — the same
2 CONT person showing the same offset twice, in two acts eight years apart, is a
2 CONT birth-year-subtraction convention, not two independent errors. This record's own
2 CONT confidence stays `sup`, since her own birth is still index-only — the `doc` grade attaches
2 CONT to this specific parent-naming, read off a primary image.
2 CONT
2 CONT **ALSO NAMED MOTHER-OF-THE-BRIDE IN THE 1907 MARRIAGE ACT, DOC-GRADE.** Emma's own 1907
2 CONT Oostende marriage act ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`) names her again, *"zonder
2 CONT beroep"* (no occupation stated there — a later-life change from *kantwerkster*, flagged
2 CONT rather than treated as a contradiction) — consenting not in person but by a separate act
2 CONT passed at Diksmuide on 8 September 1907, since she did not travel to Oostende. This
2 CONT confirms she was alive in September 1907, consistent with this record's held death year of
2 CONT 1914, and is a second, independent primary-image corroboration of the parent link, in a
2 CONT different register from the birth act, 27 years apart.
2 CONT
2 CONT SEVEN MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from a province-wide sweep of the
2 CONT vrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) for Diksmuide, each act naming both
2 CONT parents in full: [[vincke_charles_1871]] (b. 1871), [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (b. 1873),
2 CONT [[vincke_irma_1874]] (b. 1874), [[vincke_camilla_1876]] (b. 1876), [[vincke_eugene_1877]] (b. 1877),
2 CONT [[vincke_emma_1880]] (b. 1880, already held) and [[vincke_jerome_1886]] (b. 1886, aged 40.8 at his
2 CONT birth — the upper end of childbearing but not implausible). See [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record
2 CONT for the act numbers and the two independent filters that found no rival couple.
2 CONT
2 CONT An EIGHTH CHILD, [[vincke_florence_1869]] (b. Diksmuide 1869), is grafted from her own 1893
2 CONT marriage act rather than a birth act — see [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s record for why. This joins
2 CONT the couple's line to the De Keyser/Bocklandt branch of this tree (objective 3).
2 CONT
