1 REFN vandewalle_simonne
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Simonne /Vandewalle/
2 GIVN Simonne
2 SURN Vandewalle
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1913 AND 1914
2 PLAC Oostende?
1 FAMS @F91@
1 NOTE Source detail: Family (confirmed maiden name). Oostende candidates: Simonne Florida Vandewalle 1913 & Simonne Augusta 1914 — West-Vlaanderen civil birth acts (Geneanet)
2 CONT
2 CONT RESEARCH NOTE. Vandewalle is one of the most common West-Flemish surnames, so isolating her needs a linking record. Two strong Oostende candidates of the right age: (a) Simonne Florida Vandewalle, b. 6 Jun 1913 Oostende — parents Petrus Franciscus Antonius Vandewalle (1884) & Magdalena Clementia Willaert (1888); grandparents Franciscus Eduardus Vandewalle × Mathildis Vandierendounck and Emilius Willaert (1856) × Maria Lauwereins (1856–1893); (b) Simonne Augusta Vandewalle, b. 1914 Oostende. Neither is yet tied to Gustaaf. Decisive record: the Gustaaf × Simonne marriage (Oostende ~1938–40, or England 1940–43) — it would name her parents — or Roland’s 1943 UK birth (mother’s maiden name).
2 CONT
2 CONT CHECKED, AND THE CORPUS DOES NOT HAVE HER (July 2026). Her best candidate scores 27 bits
2 CONT and is **Alice Marie Van de Walle**, who was bearing Dekeyser children at Mariakerke in 1904
2 CONT and 1907 — a decade before our Simonne was born. She is not a candidate at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT What made the score is worth understanding, because it will recur on this line: the
2 CONT agreement is "surname Vandewalle" plus "child names", and the child-name agreement amounts
2 CONT to *her children were surnamed Dekeyser too*. A Vandewalle woman with Dekeyser children is
2 CONT the shape of our Simonne, but in West-Vlaanderen it is also the shape of a great many other
2 CONT women — Vandewalle and Dekeyser are both among the commonest surnames in the province. No
2 CONT date and no place agreed. Nothing grafted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her identity still turns on the record her own note names: the Gustaaf x Simonne marriage,
2 CONT or Roland's 1943 English birth certificate with the mother's maiden name.
1 SOUR @S76@
2 QUAY 1
