2 CONT by that table. The identity does not depend on the fold: the father's rare full name
2 CONT ("Eduardus Ludovicus Rudolphus Van Iseghem") plus the exact birth-date match already give
2 CONT two identifiers. Recorded as a variant, not resolved into `forenames.json`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Both parents are recorded "Ongehuwd" (unmarried), aged 25** — [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] (b.
2 CONT 29/11/1880) turning 25 on the very day of this death, [[vincke_emma_1880]] (b. 23/01/1880)
2 CONT already 25 — consistent with the couple's own 1907 marriage two years later, not a
2 CONT contradiction. This **dates the relationship to at least 1905**, bearing on the open
2 CONT legitimation frontier on [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]'s record (born Lens 1903) and [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]]'s
2 CONT (born Diksmuide 1898, under the surname Vincke) — see those records.
2 CONT
2 CONT A second son of the same forenames, [[vaniseghem_camillus_1911]], was born six years later,
2 CONT in 1911 — his own fate is still open; no death act for him has been found in this venue.
