1 NOTE Around 1903 the family was living in Lens, northern France (son Joannes was born there); father of at least seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a husband: named as the partner on [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s
2 CONT memorial-card record. She died in 1974, nearly thirty years after him, and the card still
2 CONT names him — which is how a widow's card usually reads, and it confirms the marriage from a
2 CONT source outside the trees.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from a sweep of the vrijwilligersrab
2 CONT Huwelijken index (`rab-bs-huwelijken`): [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] (m. Stene 1920), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]]
2 CONT (m. Oostende 1927), [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] (m. Stene 1931) and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]] (m. Stene 1935) —
2 CONT each act naming both parents identically to this record, alongside [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] himself,
2 CONT whose own 1928 marriage act turned up in the same sweep (see his record). None of the four
2 CONT acts gives a birth date, so none is recorded on these children. Three in-laws named only
2 CONT by the act — Desire Camille Gunst, Petrus Theodorus Carolus Joye, Joseph Louis Zwaenepoel
2 CONT — are left for a later pass rather than entered as records now.
2 CONT
2 CONT **BIRTH PLACE AND OWN CITATION SUPPLIED (2026-07-27).** His own birth row — Oostende, act
2 CONT nr. 763, RAB ID 1486308, FamilySearch waypoint QZ9J-GG1 — reads Birth Date 29/11/1880
2 CONT (the Birth Date column itself, not the Certificate Date, which is blank on this row),
2 CONT matching this record to the day and giving `birth.place` for the first time. It is one of
2 CONT eight rows this couple has in this index — see [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] for the full sibship and
2 CONT the parent-pair identifier that grounds all eight, six new siblings ([[vaniseghem_arthur_1874]],
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_augustus_1875]], [[vaniseghem_leontius]], [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]], [[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]], [[vaniseghem_ludovicus_1888]],
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_joannes_1891]]) now on file.
2 CONT
2 CONT **[[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]], already held as a child of this marriage — not a new find —
2 CONT now also has a death act on his own record (2026-07-27); see that record.**
2 CONT
2 CONT **HIS OWN MARRIAGE ACT READ AS A REGISTER IMAGE (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.** The 1907
2 CONT Oostende act itself ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`) confirms his birth to the
2 CONT day (Oostende, 29 November 1880), gives his occupation for the first time as ***werkman***
2 CONT (labourer, the new occupation field above), and states he produced his militia
2 CONT certificate. His parents [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] and [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] are both present and
2 CONT consenting and both signed. Banns were published at Oostende on Sunday 8 September 1907;
2 CONT the officer was Ernestus Van Glabbeke, schepen gedelegeerden; and the act carries **no
2 CONT marginal annotation of any kind** — no divorce note, no later correction. This is an
2 CONT independent primary source, 26 years apart from his father's 1933 death act, for the same
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] × [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] parent link.
2 CONT
2 CONT NEW FRONTIER, NOT LINKED (2026-07-27). The same act names a witness, **Eugenius De Roo**,
2 CONT 40, *kleermaker*, of Oostende, stated as *"oom van den echtgenoot"* — an uncle of the
2 CONT groom — implying a sibling of one of his parents, [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] or [[janssen_hermanie_1853]],
2 CONT married a De Roo, or a De Roo/Deroo married into one of those families directly. No
2 CONT person record, label or prior search anywhere in this tree mentions "De Roo". Not linked;
2 CONT recorded as a named frontier only.
