1 REFN vaniseghem_joannes_1852
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Joannes /Van Iseghem/
2 GIVN Joannes
2 SURN Van Iseghem
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 SEP 1852
2 PLAC Oostende
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 NOV 1933
2 PLAC Stene
1 OCCU herbergier (innkeeper)
1 FAMS @F129@
1 FAMC @F117@
1 NOTE Lived to 81; born in the city of Oostende but died in neighbouring rural Stene, where the family had settled.
2 CONT
2 CONT **THE IDENTIFIER FOR THIS WHOLE SIBSHIP (2026-07-27).** "Joannes Vaniseghem" is not, by
2 CONT itself, a name that picks out one man in this venue: grouping every VANISEGHEM Joannes
2 CONT father row in the province-wide birth index by the named mother turns up **at least nine
2 CONT different men recorded identically as "Joannes Vaniseghem"**, each paired with a different
2 CONT wife — Piesens Sophia, Werbrouck Barbara, Dekegelaere Philippina, Demeyer Maria, Carette
2 CONT Virginia, Lycke Isabelle, Vanhaecke Justine/Christina, and this record's own Hermanie
2 CONT (Hermania/Hermina) Ludovica Janssen. The father's forename alone is therefore not an
2 CONT identifier here — **the pair, both parents' full names written in full, is the
2 CONT two-identifier minimum**, and it holds for the eight birth rows below: no row anywhere in
2 CONT the province pairs "Joannes" with any mother but Hermania/Hermina Ludovica Janssen.
2 CONT
2 CONT **HIS OWN MARRIAGE ACT** — Oostende, 23 August 1872, act nr. 93, RAB ID 582203, microfilm
2 CONT 4794599 — names both spouses in full and gives both their birth dates exactly as already
2 CONT held (groom 25/09/1852, bride 05/07/1853 — see [[janssen_hermanie_1853]]), where previously
2 CONT both rested on the single Geneanet tree `tree-gverdievel` alone. It also names all four
2 CONT parents — VANISEGHEM Joannes Josephus x GAUTIERT Anna Maria, and JANSSEN Josephus Joannes
2 CONT x HUYGHEBAERT Appolonia Joanna — matching this tree's held [[vaniseghem_joannes_1819]] x
2 CONT [[gautiert_anna_1819]] and [[janssen_josephus_1820]] x [[huyghebaert_appolonia_1830]] exactly, and gives
2 CONT the previous generation's own deaths (see those four records), independently
2 CONT re-confirming dates a separate pass recorded the same day.
2 CONT
2 CONT **HIS OWN DEATH ACT** — Stene, 13 November 1933, act nr. 40, RAB ID 2184011 — is the only
2 CONT source in this tree stating the [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] → [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] link **in a civil act's
2 CONT own words**: the Detail's own Birth Date field (25/09/1852, Oostende) matches this record
2 CONT to the day, and the two comparants are family, each stating their own relation —
2 CONT "VANISEGHEM Eduard, 50, boodschapper, Stene, *zoon*" and "VANISEGHEM Joannes, 30,
2 CONT werkman, Stene, *kleinzoon*". The son is [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] (whose 1901 brother's own
2 CONT marriage act separately gives him the same trade, *boodschapper*); the grandson, aged 30
2 CONT in 1933, fits [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] (b. 11/05/1903) almost exactly — a second, previously
2 CONT unclaimed corroboration of the three-generation chain, alongside the stated one. Eduard's
2 CONT declared age, 50, is stated two years light — he turned 53 sixteen days after this act —
2 CONT a declarant's rounded age, flagged rather than smoothed over. Widowerhood is stated to
2 CONT "JANSSEN Hermania Ludovica" in the Previous Partners table, matching [[janssen_hermanie_1853]].
2 CONT His own birth act (Oostende, act nr 763 — see [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]) is a fourth Van Iseghem
2 CONT sibling generation removed and is not this act; both remain index rows, not images, so
2 CONT confidence stays `sup`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A THIRD, INDEPENDENT PRIMARY SOURCE FOR THE SAME LINK (2026-07-27), DOC-GRADE.** His son
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]'s own 1907 marriage act, read as a register image
2 CONT ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), names him present and
2 CONT consenting, and gives his occupation for the first time as ***herbergier*** (innkeeper,
2 CONT the new occupation field above). This is 26 years earlier than his own 1933 death act
2 CONT above, and a different register from both it and his birth act — a third, wholly
2 CONT independent primary attestation of the same [[vaniseghem_joannes_1852]] × [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] →
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] link. This record's own vital dates remain index-only, so confidence stays
2 CONT `sup`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **EIGHT CHILDREN with [[janssen_hermanie_1853]], all from the RAB birth index and cross-filed
2 CONT from her own record too, so no ninth exists on either side:** [[vaniseghem_arthur_1874]] (17/03/1874),
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_augustus_1875]] (13/08/1875, d. in infancy), [[vaniseghem_leontius]] (registered 1876, no birth
2 CONT date recovered), [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]] (05/01/1878), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] (29/11/1880, already held),
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]] (21/03/1883, d. in infancy), [[vaniseghem_ludovicus_1888]] (20/02/1888, d. in
2 CONT infancy) and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1891]] (16/05/1891). Filtering the province-wide index separately
2 CONT by father-name and by [[janssen_hermanie_1853]]'s own surname returns the identical eight RAB
2 CONT IDs {1486295, 1486298, 1486308, 1486318, 1486324, 1486325, 1486336, 2042291} — no rival
2 CONT couple, no ninth child from either filter. Three further spellings (Vaniseghem, Van
2 CONT Yseghem, Vaniseghen) were tried against the sibship: "Vaniseghem" returned the identical
2 CONT 1568 rows as "Van Iseghem" (byte counts differ only by the echoed search string);
2 CONT "Van Yseghem" is a genuinely different key (25 rows, none this family); "Vaniseghen"
2 CONT returns zero. **Not independently verified**: whether "Vaniseghem" and two-word
2 CONT "Van Iseghem" are byte-for-byte identical could not be checked, because only the
2 CONT one-word capture was kept in scratch — recorded as unconfirmed, not as proven.
2 CONT
2 CONT **TWO UNNAMED INFANT DEATHS, NOT GRAFTED — no name, no id, no file (CLAUDE.md rule 5).**
2 CONT Oostende, 18/11/1878, act nr. 626, RAB ID 264403: Sex M, born Oostende, Christinastraat
2 CONT 72, no age given; father comparant "VANISEGHEM Joannes, 26, Werkman … vader" and mother
2 CONT 25 — both ages consistent with this couple in 1878. And Oostende, 06/11/1879, act nr.
2 CONT 570, RAB ID 266409: Detail entirely blank. Both are transcribed with "Sn" (no forename)
2 CONT in the Deceased field. **"Sn" is a name-position code, not a sex marker** — the codes
2 CONT compound ("VANISEGHEM Sn Vr", "DEVLOO Sn Ml"), so Sn means registered without a forename
2 CONT and Ml/Vr (manlijk/vrouwelijk) carry the sex separately; the venue's own Vocabularium does
2 CONT not define the code, this is read off the corpus itself. Of 71 such rows scanned
2 CONT province-wide across the Van Iseghem and Janssen result sets, only **33 reproduce** on a
2 CONT second read; the other 38 could not be reproduced and are not claimed. Not one of the 33
2 CONT names a Partner and most name both parents — the signature of a newborn registration, not
2 CONT an adult's. Recorded as **"unnamed child"**, not "stillborn": the death Detail form has no
2 CONT "Stillborn" field at all (only the birth form does), so that distinction needs the
2 CONT register image, not this index. The hypothesis that the 1878 row is [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]] dying
2 CONT at ten months is **rejected**: every other child of this couple who died after being
2 CONT named appears in this index *under that name* (see [[vaniseghem_augustus_1875]], [[vaniseghem_joannes_1883]],
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_ludovicus_1888]] below), so the venue's own demonstrated convention is that a named child
2 CONT is transcribed by name — "Sn" is consistent only with a child never named.
2 CONT
2 CONT **TWO STILL OPEN — [[vaniseghem_leontius]] and [[vaniseghem_gustavus_1878]] have no death and no marriage in
2 CONT this venue.** Scope actually covered: Oostende deaths 1800–1939; Stene carries only 2 rows
2 CONT for this surname in the whole file (1933, 1936), too thin to confirm or refute a death
2 CONT there before 1915; marriages 1872–1936; both parent-side filters run each time. Four
2 CONT alternatives remain open, none closed: death after 1939; death at Stene before 1915;
2 CONT death outside West-Vlaanderen entirely — this family demonstrably moved, since
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]]'s son [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] was born at Lens, France; or an unmatched name-form.
2 CONT
2 CONT **"No unrecorded daughter" is narrowed, not established.** "Hermania Ludovica" appears
2 CONT exactly 5 times in the province-wide marriage file — once as a bride, four times as
2 CONT "Mother of the Groom", never as "Mother of the Bride". That is a real finding, but it
2 CONT overreaches to call it a closed enumeration: this couple is shown above to have had at
2 CONT least one child (perhaps two) die before ever being named — exactly what a marriage
2 CONT sweep cannot catch. Recorded as **"no unrecorded daughter who lived to marry within this
2 CONT venue's window"**, not as "ruled out".
2 CONT
2 CONT **A curiosity, explicitly weightless.** [[janssen_hermanie_1853]] died 13/11/1926 and this
2 CONT record 13/11/1933 — seven years to the day. A frequency check across all 1,521 dated rows
2 CONT in the relevant result sets shows 13/11 occurring 7 times, in line with the base rate for
2 CONT other day/month pairs (9–12 occurrences each). Genuine, but not evidence of anything —
2 CONT recorded so a later pass does not mistake coincidence for a fact.
