1 NOTE Born in the French coal-mining town of Lens, where his Oostende family had emigrated for work; the family later returned to Belgium. Died six days short of his 66th birthday.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED (July 2026) by a Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record:
2 CONT born **Lens** 11 May 1903, died Oostende 5 May 1969, partner Adrienne Devriendt. The
2 CONT birthplace is the striking part — an Oostende family with a son born at Lens — and the
2 CONT card gives it independently of the trees, which is the strongest single reason to believe
2 CONT this is the same man. This record notes Lens as being in France; the card says only
2 CONT "Lens" — which Lens was not settled by the card, but is settled below by his parents' own
2 CONT 1907 marriage act.
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE DATED (2026-07-27): his own marriage act — Stene nr. 6, 24 March 1928
2 CONT (vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index, `rab-bs-huwelijken`) — names his parents in full as
2 CONT Eduardus Van Iseghem × Emma Celesta Vincke, matching this tree's existing
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] × [[vincke_emma_1880]] exactly, and the bride's parents as Devriendt Eugenius
2 CONT Alphonsius × Schalandryn Octavia Maria, matching [[devriendt_eugenius_1882]] × [[schalandrijn_octavia_1886]]
2 CONT exactly. Both couples were already held in this tree as his and Adrienne's parents; this
2 CONT act corroborates an already-fully-linked marriage and supplies the date and place that
2 CONT were previously missing from both records, not a new tree collapse.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — an unexplained gap of over four years. His held birth, 11 May 1903 at Lens,
2 CONT precedes his parents' held marriage, 28 September 1907, by more than four years. Either
2 CONT an earlier, unregistered union or a later legitimation would explain it — this tree
2 CONT already carries the second pattern elsewhere (see [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s marriage to Louise
2 CONT Bocklandt, which legitimized two children already born). Left open; neither date is
2 CONT altered here.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A second data point for the same pattern (2026-07-27).** A birth-index sweep for rows
2 CONT naming [[vincke_emma_1880]] as mother, incidental to an unrelated blind-window pass, turned up
2 CONT two more births registered to her alone before the 1907 marriage, father NN NN: "VINCKE
2 CONT Flavie Eulalie" (b. 1898, matching [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]]'s rare forename pair) and "VINCKE Albert
2 CONT Joseph" (b. 1899, d. 1900). If either was legitimized by the 1907 marriage, that would be
2 CONT the same mechanism that would explain this record's own Lens-1903 gap. **NOT PROVEN,
2 CONT not grafted** — it needs the marriage act's own legitimation field read (see
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]]'s record for the exact query handle). Recorded here as the same open
2 CONT question, not resolved by it.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A third data point (2026-07-27).** [[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]]'s own death act (Oostende,
2 CONT 29/11/1905) records both his parents as "Ongehuwd", aged 25 — i.e. still unmarried in
2 CONT late 1905, two years before their actual wedding. This independently dates the
2 CONT relationship to at least 1905, sitting between the 1898/1899 Vincke-surnamed births above
2 CONT and this record's own 1903 Lens birth. It strengthens the pattern without proving the
2 CONT legitimation hypothesis: the marriage act's own legitimation field still has not been
2 CONT read.
2 CONT
2 CONT **RESOLVED (2026-07-27) — RECORD UPGRADED `sup` → `doc`.** The parents' own 1907 marriage
2 CONT act, read as a register image ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), carries a legitimation
2 CONT clause naming him directly: "en Joannes Van Yseghem, geboren te Lens, in Frankryk, den
2 CONT elfden Mei negentien honderd en drie" — 11 May 1903, **Lens, in France**, in the
2 CONT register's own words. This settles both open questions on this record at once: which Lens
2 CONT (the act states it explicitly), and the four-year gap before the parents' marriage — this
2 CONT is a **legitimation of a child already born**, the same mechanism as [[dekeyser_edouard_1876]]'s
2 CONT marriage elsewhere in this tree, not an unrecorded earlier union. His siblings
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] and [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] are named in the identical clause on the identical
2 CONT terms; see their records.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A CHILD NOT IN THE TREE, NOT GRAFTED (2026-07-27).** A death-index sweep turned up "VAN
2 CONT ISEGHEM Roger Bernard", Stene, 27/02/1929, act nr. 10, RAB ID 2148819 — father "VAN
2 CONT ISEGHEM Joannes", mother "DEVRIENDT Adrienne Margaretha", both written in full, matching
2 CONT this couple exactly and sitting eleven months after their 24/03/1928 marriage. Two
2 CONT identifiers (both parents' full names) are present, but **no Detail view was fetched for
2 CONT this row** — no sex, no birth date, no age — so nothing beyond his existence and
2 CONT parentage can be stated, and no record is created. What would settle it: the Detail page,
2 CONT GET `/en/node/172` on RAB ID 2148819. He would predate [[vaniseghem_rosette]], [[vaniseghem_diane]] and
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_edi]] if confirmed.
