2 CONT marriage act — Stene nr. 21, 17 August 1935 (vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index,
2 CONT `rab-bs-huwelijken`) — names her parents in full as Eduardus Van Iseghem x Emma Celesta
2 CONT Vincke, matching this couple exactly; one of five such acts spanning 1920-1935 that all
2 CONT converge on the identical parent-name pair. Index only, not the register image, hence
2 CONT `sup`. The marriage act does not give her own birth date.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Birth date (2026-07-27), NOT INDEPENDENTLY RE-CHECKED.** A birth-index sweep for rows
2 CONT naming [[vincke_emma_1880]] as mother turned up her own row: Oostende act nr. 80, 22 January
2 CONT 1913 (`rab-bs-geboorten`). The verifier did not itself confirm this date against a second
2 CONT act or memorial card, and this same index's "Date"/"Certificate Date" columns are
2 CONT confirmed elsewhere in this family to be conflated (see `rab-bs-overlijdens`'s note and
2 CONT the corrections on [[vincke_irma_1874]] and [[vincke_jerome_1886]]) — recorded with that caveat
2 CONT rather than left out, since the row cites a specific act number.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — her husband. The same index names him **Joseph Louis Zwaenepoel**, but he has
2 CONT no record of his own here: this pass is naming [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s
2 CONT children, not their in-laws, so his own record is left for objective 2's next pass rather
2 CONT than entered now.
