1 REFN vermandel_ida_1825
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Ida /Vermandel/
2 GIVN Ida
2 SURN Vermandel
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1825
2 PLAC Zelzate
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 JUN 1865
2 PLAC Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen)
1 OCCU arbeidster (labourer)
1 FAMS @F197@
1 NOTE Maternal grandmother of Louise Bocklandt; wife of Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ACT READ (2026-07-26) — **Hamme death act nr. 123, 1865**, read as the register image. She
2 CONT had been in this tree with a bare year at each end and no place at all. The act gives:
2 CONT
2 CONT > …dat gisteren, den een en twintigsten Juny, om half negen uren 's avonds, **Ida
2 CONT > Vermandel**, oud negen en dertig jaren, *arbeidster*, **geboortig van Zeltzaete**,
2 CONT > wonende te Hamme, **huisvrouw van Joannes Franciscus Van Bergen**, dochter van nog
2 CONT > levende […] Vermandel en van […] Verplancken, overleden is in het burgerhospitael…
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on **21 June 1865** at Hamme, in the town hospital on the Marktplein, aged
2 CONT thirty-nine and working as a labourer. Two identifiers carry the identification and neither
2 CONT is her name: the commune, which [[vanbergen_marielouise_1842]]'s 1888 Oostende death act independently
2 CONT gives as where Ida died, and her husband's full name, matching [[vanbergen_joannes_1815]] exactly.
2 CONT *Ida Vermandel* is in any case close to unique — the only other in the whole Open Archives
2 CONT index is a 1949 death in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Her birthplace is Zelzate, not Waasmunster**, and that needs stating carefully, because
2 CONT §56 had just moved this family's assumed origin from Hamme to Waasmunster on her daughter's
2 CONT evidence. Both are true and they are two different people: Marie-Louise was born at
2 CONT Waasmunster in 1842, Ida at Zelzate around 1825. Zelzate is not in the Waasland at all — it
2 CONT is on the Dutch border north of Gent. Her own birth act and her parents are therefore in
2 CONT the **Zelzate** registers, and the marriage could be in any of three communes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her age, thirty-nine in June 1865, puts her birth between June 1825 and June 1826. The held
2 CONT `1825` survives that without being confirmed by it, so the year stays as it was.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — **her parents are named in this act and are deliberately not recorded.** It says
2 CONT they were *nog levende*, still living, in June 1865, which is itself a search constraint.
2 CONT But the forenames do not survive magnification: the father's is a looped capital followed
2 CONT by *-rimus*, where P, F and S are all plausible against the same clerk's *Petrus* and
2 CONT *Franciscus* elsewhere on the page, and the mother's renders as something between
2 CONT *Josephina* and *Delphina*. The surnames are legible — **Vermandel** and **Verplancken**.
2 CONT A forename read at the edge of legibility is exactly the guess this project has no syntax
2 CONT for, so nothing is written. Her Zelzate birth act settles both, and the Zelzate registers
2 CONT are mapped: `fs-zelzate-civil-registers-1796-1870`, with a ten-year table covering
2 CONT 1802–1870 (DGS 005089047) that turns it into a single lookup.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER — two more probable children, index-level only and not grafted: **Josephus**
2 CONT (b. 1852, m. Clementina Van Buyten at Hamme 1911, d. Hamme 27 October 1927) and **Henricus**
2 CONT (b. 1861, d. Hamme 2 May 1919), both indexed with this mother and a father *Franciscus*.
2 CONT Their own acts have not been read. [[vandenberghe_paulina_1849]] stood in exactly that position until
2 CONT her 1882 act was opened, which is the argument for opening theirs.
1 SOUR @S149@
2 QUAY 3
