1 OCCU ijzersmit (blacksmith)
1 FAMS @F198@
1 FAMC @F195@
1 NOTE Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — found
2 CONT one year **outside** the 1866-1870 blind window this pass was sent to close, while
2 CONT sweeping the marriage index for the window's children. His own birth, Diksmuide 1865 act
2 CONT nr. 202, falls just before it: the couple married 24 May 1865, so this is barely four
2 CONT months on.
2 CONT
2 CONT His marriage — Diksmuide, 19 September 1888, act nr. 149 (`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — gives
2 CONT him born Diksmuide 13 September 1865, age 23, *ijzersmit*, and names his parents in full
2 CONT as Vincke Lucianus Julianus (48, metser) × Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria (43,
2 CONT kantwerkster) — matching this couple exactly and matching birth act nr. 202 to the day.
2 CONT Independently corroborated from the local corpus, not the same register: a Familiekunde
2 CONT Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card (`fwk-alfons-vincke`,
2 CONT `fwk:bb261d5b-e241-84c8-0c3c-860a943cca23`) gives his birth as 13 September 1865 and names
2 CONT the same spouse, Eugenia Vandecappelle.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Flagged plainly, not smoothed over:** he was born 3 months 20 days after his parents'
2 CONT 24 May 1865 wedding — conception preceding the marriage by roughly five months, which is
2 CONT sometimes the reason for the marriage rather than a contradiction of it. Neither date is
2 CONT adjusted.
2 CONT
2 CONT His own birth act and 1888 marriage act remain index only, not the register image.
2 CONT
2 CONT **THE SIBLING LINK ITSELF UPGRADED TO `doc` (2026-07-27).** His sister [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s
2 CONT own 1907 marriage act, read as a register image
2 CONT ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), carries him as a witness,
2 CONT in the register's own words: *"Alphonsus Vincke, oud twee en veertig jaren, stoofmaker,
2 CONT broeder der echtgenoote"* — 42 years old, stoofmaker, **brother of the bride**. Two
2 CONT identifiers agree in this one primary image: his stated age matches his held birth date
2 CONT to the exact day (he turned 42 fifteen days before the 28 September 1907 act), and the act
2 CONT **states the sibling relationship directly**, rather than it being inferred only from the
2 CONT separately-held parent records that grafted him here at `sup` (research-log §67). His
2 CONT occupation there, *stoofmaker*, differs from *ijzersmit* on his own 1888 marriage act — a
2 CONT plausible 19-year career change, flagged rather than treated as a contradiction. His own
2 CONT birth act is still unread as an image, so only the sibling identification itself carries
2 CONT `doc`.
1 SOUR @S152@
