1 REFN vincke_emma_1880
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Emma Celesta /Vincke/
2 GIVN Emma Celesta
2 SURN Vincke
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 JAN 1880
2 PLAC Diksmuide
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 OCT 1974
2 PLAC Oostende
1 FAMS @F208@
1 FAMC @F195@
1 NOTE Lived to 94 — the longest-lived in this cluster — outliving her husband by nearly 30 years. Daughter of Lucien Vincke & Ludovica Vanalderweireldt.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record gives
2 CONT her birth at Diksmuide on 23 January 1880, her death at Oostende on 6 October 1974, and
2 CONT her partner as Eduard Van Iseghem — every field as held here, and the marriage to
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] with it. She had rested on the gverdievel tree alone.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her birth act is Diksmuide **akte nr. 14, act date 24 January 1880**, child *Emma Celesta
2 CONT Vincke*, born Diksmuide 23 January 1880 — one day before the act date, the ordinary gap
2 CONT between a birth and its declaration — naming her parents [[vincke_lucien_1840]] ×
2 CONT [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]. The act id is GEWVL_GEBWVL_01583386. Its AGATHA index transcription
2 CONT is held as `data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-diksmuide.md`
2 CONT ([[agatha-diksmuide-1880-birth-emma-vincke]]) and **stays `sup`** — see below for why.
2 CONT
2 CONT **THE REGISTER IMAGE READ (2026-07-27) — UPGRADES THIS RECORD `sup` → `doc`.** FamilySearch
2 CONT image group **004833210**, image **392 of 1269**, ark `3:1:33SQ-GPD9-32V`
2 CONT ([[fs-diksmuide-civil-registers-film-004833210]]) is the register page itself, held as
2 CONT `data/artifacts/emma-vincke-1880-birth-act-image.md`. It supersedes the AGATHA index
2 CONT transcription above, which is kept alongside it rather than discarded — one is the primary
2 CONT act, the other its independent index precursor, and both remain useful. Two identifiers
2 CONT are now read directly off the image: birth date + place (23 January 1880, Diksmuide) and
2 CONT both parents' full names, Lucien Julianus Vincke × Ludovica Maria Vanalderweireldt.
2 CONT
2 CONT **New facts the image gives that no index held:** the birth hour, **3 a.m.**; the
2 CONT address — the father's own dwelling on the **Kleinendyk**, Diksmuide; the father's trade
2 CONT in the register's own hand, ***metsersdiender*** (the tree held "metserdiener" from a
2 CONT member tree — the act writes it with the linking -s-; see [[vincke_lucien_1840]]); and
2 CONT [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]]'s occupation, ***kantwerkster*** (lacemaker), not previously held
2 CONT anywhere. The declaring officer was **Edmond Paret**, schepen.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Two objections were raised against the match, and both are defeated — recorded, not
2 CONT smoothed over.** First: both parents' stated ages are one year high — 40 and 35, where
2 CONT they were 39y10m and 34y2m by this tree's held birth dates. The identical +1 offset
2 CONT recurs on [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] alone in a wholly separate document, her 1888 Alfons Vincke
2 CONT marriage act (43 stated vs 42 completed, where Lucien's own age there is uninformative
2 CONT because his birthday had already passed) — one person showing the same offset twice, in
2 CONT two acts eight years and one register apart, is a birth-year-subtraction convention (the
2 CONT age reached *during* that year, not the age completed at declaration), not two independent
2 CONT errors, and it does not unseat either held birth date. Second: the mother's surname was
2 CONT flagged as not letter-by-letter certain on first read. Re-cropped at 6× zoom in three
2 CONT passes: the **R after `-ALD-`** is clearly present — ruling out the `VANDERWEIRELT`
2 CONT no-R variant that hid records elsewhere in this family — and the final cluster reads
2 CONT **`-eldt`**, tighter than the artifact's own original caveat (corrected there too).
2 CONT
2 CONT **The venue fact, now confirmed logged in, not merely index-derived.** AGATHA (as user
2 CONT `shbunder`) publishes **no scan link at all** for its West-Vlaanderen birth project — every
2 CONT `<a>` on act GEWVL_GEBWVL_01583386 was tested for image/scan/mirador/iiif, zero matches —
2 CONT so the earlier finding that the act's own page carries no route to the image is structural,
2 CONT not a session artifact. And AGATHA's own remark on the act, **"SCAN 392 GSU"**, is exactly
2 CONT FamilySearch's frame 392 on film 004833210 — the bridge AGATHA itself does not publish.
2 CONT
2 CONT CORROBORATED INDEPENDENTLY by her own marriage act — Oostende, 28 September 1907, act nr.
2 CONT 212 (RAB ID 668717, FamilySearch film 004166052 image i=138) — which names her parents the
2 CONT same way, Vincke Lucien Julianus × Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria. First read from the
2 CONT vrijwilligersrab Huwelijken index (`rab-bs-huwelijken`), where it was real corroboration —
2 CONT a different commune, register and volunteer batch from the birth-act transcription — but
2 CONT **not independent of AGATHA in its birth-side pairing**: the vrijwilligersrab BIRTH row for
2 CONT this same act shares AGATHA's own hidden act id, 1583386 (GEWVL_GEBWVL_01583386), the same
2 CONT Rijksarchief volunteer transcription seen twice, not a second source. **Now also read as
2 CONT the register image itself** ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`), doc-grade and genuinely
2 CONT independent of the birth-act image — different register, date and clerk — confirming the
2 CONT same parent names and her birth date and place to the day.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from the same Huwelijken sweep:
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] (m. Stene 1920), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] (m. Oostende 1927), [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]]
2 CONT (m. Stene 1931) and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]] (m. Stene 1935) — each act naming both parents
2 CONT identically to this record, alongside [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]] himself, whose own 1928 marriage act
2 CONT turned up in the same sweep (see his record).
2 CONT
2 CONT TWO MORE CHILDREN, WITH A CAVEAT (2026-07-27): a birth-index sweep for rows naming this
2 CONT record as mother turned up two more Oostende children of [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1880]] × this record —
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]] (b. 25 April 1905, act nr. 501) and [[vaniseghem_camillus_1911]]
2 CONT (b. 6 January 1911, act nr. 14) — and birth dates for three already-held children,
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] (2 November 1901), [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] (23 March 1909) and [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]]
2 CONT (22 January 1913). [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]]'s date is no longer uncorroborated: the 1907 marriage
2 CONT act's own legitimation clause, below, independently confirms it. [[vaniseghem_valentina_1909]] and
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_maria_1913]]'s dates remain not independently re-checked against a second act.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE LEGITIMATION CLAUSE READ (2026-07-27) — RESOLVES THE TWO-BIRTHS-BEFORE-MARRIAGE
2 CONT FRONTIER, IN PART. The 1907
2 CONT marriage act's own legitimation clause ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]])
2 CONT names exactly three children as this couple's legitimate issue: [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] (b.
2 CONT Diksmuide 26 March 1898), [[vaniseghem_eduardus_1901]] (b. Oostende 2 November 1901) and [[vaniseghem_joannes_1903]]
2 CONT (b. Lens, France, 11 May 1903) — see each record. "VINCKE Flavie Eulalie" of 26 March 1898
2 CONT is [[vaniseghem_flavie_1898]] herself, tied by forename pair, day, month, year and commune, not by act
2 CONT reference (the 1907 act cites no birth act number). "VINCKE Albert Joseph" (b. 9 December
2 CONT 1899, d. 26 March 1900) is **named by neither the legitimation clause nor any other act**:
2 CONT the clause names three children and no others, and both his death and
2 CONT [[vaniseghem_camillus_1905]]'s (d. 1905) predate the 1907 wedding, the ordinary reason a
2 CONT legitimation passes over an already-dead infant. The act is silent on him, not contrary —
2 CONT his paternity **stays unproven and unlinked**; see [[vincke_romanie_1873]] for a separate,
2 CONT explicitly-speculative lead this same act raised and did not settle.
1 SOUR @S153@
