2 CONT Oostende marriage act ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]],
2 CONT `data/artifacts/vaniseghem-vincke-1907-marriage-oostende.md`) names him again, present and
2 CONT consenting: *"Lucien Julianus, werkman"* — a plain labourer, a further occupation change
2 CONT from *metsersdiender* (1880) and *metser* (Alfons's 1888 marriage act), flagged as a
2 CONT plausible career shift over 27 years rather than a contradiction. This is a second,
2 CONT independent primary-image corroboration of the parent link, in a different register from
2 CONT the birth act, 27 years apart.
2 CONT
2 CONT SEVEN MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED (research-log §64), from a province-wide sweep of the
2 CONT vrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) for Diksmuide, each act naming both
2 CONT parents in full as Vincke Lucien Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria: [[vincke_charles_1871]]
2 CONT (b. 30 Dec 1871), [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (b. 7 Oct 1873 — one capture spells the father "Lucien
2 CONT Julien", a forename variant, not a rival father), [[vincke_irma_1874]] (b. 1 Nov 1874),
2 CONT [[vincke_camilla_1876]] (b. 20 Apr 1876), [[vincke_eugene_1877]] (b. 23 Jul 1877), [[vincke_emma_1880]]
2 CONT (b. 23 Jan 1880, already held) and [[vincke_jerome_1886]] (b. 22 Sep 1886). Filtering the same
2 CONT index separately by father's forename and by mother's rare surname returns the identical
2 CONT set — no rival couple. This closes the enumeration for Diksmuide **1871 onward**.
2 CONT
2 CONT An EIGHTH CHILD, [[vincke_florence_1869]] (b. Diksmuide 1869), is grafted separately from her
2 CONT own 1893 marriage act ([[agatha-diksmuide-1893-marriage-bocklandt-vincke]]), not from a
2 CONT birth act: Diksmuide's 1866-1870 birth rows carry only a bare father surname, no forename
2 CONT and no mother, so parentage cannot be read from the index in that window. Her marriage
2 CONT also joins this couple's line to the De Keyser/Bocklandt branch (objective 3).
2 CONT
2 CONT THE 1866-1870 BLIND WINDOW, BROKEN (research-log §67, 2026-07-27). Diksmuide births in
2 CONT those years name no parents in the index at all — but the couple's children's own LATER
2 CONT acts do, the same route that recovered Florence Amelie. Two further routes closed most of
2 CONT it: each blind-window child's own marriage act, and — crucially, because it reaches
2 CONT children who died before ever marrying — each one's own death act.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR MORE CHILDREN GRAFTED: [[vincke_theophil_1866]] (b. 1866, m. Valerie Bolle 1893, d.
2 CONT Oostende 1922 — via his own marriage AND death acts, 29 years apart, full parent-name
2 CONT agreement on both, plus a rival Theophile Achille Vincke of Diksmuide ruled out by
2 CONT parents/spouse/death year), [[vincke_bellarmin_1867]] (b. 1867, d. Diksmuide 1872, an infant —
2 CONT via his death act only, since he never married), [[vincke_karolus_1870]] (b. 1870, d.
2 CONT Diksmuide 1871, an infant, whose name was then reused for [[vincke_charles_1871]] four months
2 CONT later — via his death act only) and [[vincke_alfons_1865]] (b. 1865, one year OUTSIDE this
2 CONT window but found by the same marriage-index sweep, m. Eugenia Vandecappelle 1888,
2 CONT corroborated independently by a Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — born 3
2 CONT months 20 days after this couple's own wedding, flagged and not smoothed over).
2 CONT
2 CONT TWELVE GRANDCHILDREN, contingent on the two links above: six children of
2 CONT [[vincke_theophil_1866]] × [[bolle_valerie]] — [[vincke_marie_1894]] (1894-1895),
2 CONT [[vincke_leopold_1895]] (1895, an infant death), [[vincke_marie_1896]] (1896),
2 CONT [[vincke_madeleine_1898]] (1898-1898, an infant death), [[vincke_leopold_1900]]
2 CONT (1900-1900, the same name reused after the first died) and [[vincke_eduardus_1905]]
2 CONT (b. Oostende 1905, after the family moved there) — and six of [[vincke_alfons_1865]] ×
2 CONT [[vandecappelle_eugenia]]: [[vincke_juliette_1889]] (1889),
2 CONT [[vincke_georges_1890]] (1890), [[vincke_karel_1892]] (1892), [[vincke_louisa_1894]]
2 CONT (1894-1894, an infant death), [[vincke_camille_1895]] (b. 1895, d. Brugge 1918, his own
2 CONT death act naming his parents a second time) and [[vincke_andre_1901]] (1901).
2 CONT
2 CONT TWO EXCLUDED, deliberately not grafted. "Medard Edmond Vincke" (blind-window birth 1866
2 CONT nr. 214) is a different Vincke woman's child: his own death act (Diksmuide 1866 nr. 274)
2 CONT names father NN NN, mother Vincke Philomena Helena. "Elodie Vincke" (blind-window birth
2 CONT 1870 nr. 16) belongs to a separate, prolific Diksmuide Vincke line: her own 1894 marriage
2 CONT act names her parents as Richard Aloïs Vincke × Eugenie Dekeyrel, not this couple — a
2 CONT birth-year wobble (1870 vs 1871) on the index is immaterial, since under either year the
2 CONT parents are not ours. This clan holds two different women named Elodie: this record's
2 CONT own [[vincke_romanie_1873]] ("Romanie Elodie", act 206/1873, parents named in full) is not the
2 CONT same person as the excluded 1870 Elodie above — exactly the near-miss class CLAUDE.md's
2 CONT rule 1 exists for.
2 CONT
2 CONT FIVE STILL NOT PROVEN, a named frontier rather than a link: **Emil Fidèle** (1867 nr.
2 CONT 256), **Gustave Camil** (1867 nr. 266), **Florida Juliana** (1869 nr. 74), **Arthur
2 CONT Carolus** (1870 nr. 88) and **Cyrille Camil** (1870 nr. 69) are bare VINCKE-only rows with
2 CONT no parent-naming act found for any of them, in either the marriage or the death index.
2 CONT Scope actually covered, so the wall stays re-openable rather than closed: the whole
2 CONT West-Flemish marriage index (all communes, all years, Vincke + Vyncke, eight spellings of
2 CONT the mother's surname); the whole West-Flemish death index (Vincke, 2212 rows — Florida
2 CONT returns zero province-wide); Open Archives Belgium-wide, twelve forename queries, 75
2 CONT records. Diksmuide itself carries 26 Vincke-touching marriages 1880-1910 and 124 death
2 CONT rows 1798-1910 — the commune **is** covered; these five are absent from it, not hidden
2 CONT behind it. What would settle them is the register image behind the `SCAN nnn GSU`
2 CONT reference on the AGATHA side, or a FamilySearch session on the vrijwilligersrab arks — not
2 CONT a further index sweep. A NEW LEAD, NOT AN IDENTIFIER (2026-07-27): a witness at
2 CONT [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s 1907 marriage, Constantinus Degraeve, is stated in the act as *"zwager
2 CONT der echtgenoote"* — brother-in-law of the bride — implying a Vincke sister of hers married
2 CONT a Degraeve, possibly one of the five above, possibly [[vincke_romanie_1873]] (the one daughter
2 CONT of this couple with no further record of her own). See [[vincke_romanie_1873]]'s record: this
2 CONT is recorded as pure surname-coincidence speculation, not linked to anyone.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also ambiguous: a Nieuwkerke marriage of "VINCKE Cyrille Camille" ×
2 CONT "REUBRECHT Valerie Eugenie" (act nr. 4) is blank in every Detail field and two corpus
2 CONT memorial cards confirm the couple existed (d. 22/05/1937) but name no parents — it neither
2 CONT confirms nor refutes a link to Cyrille Camil above.
2 CONT
2 CONT AN ARGUMENT, USED ONLY TO EXCLUDE, NEVER TO INCLUDE. Diksmuide birth acts are
2 CONT strictly date-ordered (77 act-number/date pairs checked 1871-1910, zero violations), so
2 CONT act-number spacing against a known birth rate can flag an implausible gap. The birth rate
2 CONT is not constant, though — it declines from ~0.73-0.81 acts/day in the early 1870s to
2 CONT ~0.2-0.3 by 1900-1910 — and recomputed with the conservative in-period rate (~0.75), the
2 CONT gap around the 1870 acts comes out to roughly 212-237 days, still under the ~270-300-day
2 CONT floor a second full-term birth needs. This spacing argument is corroboration only, and it
2 CONT is never grounds for a graft (CLAUDE.md rule 1): it agrees with the independent exclusion
2 CONT of Medard Edmond above (~48 days' spacing, plausible only as a different mother's child,
2 CONT which his own death act already settles), and it does **not** close the excluded Elodie
2 CONT above (~282 days, borderline) — that case is settled by her own marriage act, a document,
2 CONT not by this arithmetic.
1 SOUR @S128@
2 QUAY 2
