1 NOTE Daughter of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s sister. Her
2 CONT birth — Diksmuide act nr. 206, 7 October 1873 — is one of seven Diksmuide rows in the
2 CONT vrijwilligersrab Geboorten index (`rab-bs-geboorten`) naming both parents as Vincke Lucien
2 CONT Julianus x Vanalderweireldt Ludovica Maria. Index only, not the register image, hence
2 CONT `sup`.
2 CONT
2 CONT **One capture of this act renders the father as "Lucien Julien" rather than "Lucien
2 CONT Julianus"** — every other act in this cluster, and his own record, give him the latter.
2 CONT Accepted here as a French/Latin variant of the same forename, not a different father:
2 CONT the mother's rarer full name, the commune and the chronology (she was 27.9) all agree,
2 CONT there is no evidence of Ludovica having any other husband, and the same province-wide
2 CONT sweep that closes off a rival couple for her siblings found none here either. The variant
2 CONT is flagged, not concealed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Formerly a frontier on [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s own record ("a probable second daughter, not
2 CONT grafted"); resolved here (research-log §64).
2 CONT
2 CONT NEW FRONTIER, NOT LINKED (2026-07-27). [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s own 1907 marriage act, read as a
2 CONT register image ([[fs-oostende-1907-marriage-vaniseghem-vincke]]), carries a witness
2 CONT **Constantinus Degraeve**, 36, *aardewerker*, of Diksmuide, stated in the register's own
2 CONT words as *"zwager der echtgenoote"* — brother-in-law of the bride — implying an
2 CONT **unrecorded Vincke sister married a Degraeve**. No person record, label or prior search
2 CONT anywhere in this tree mentions "Degraeve." This record is the only Vincke daughter of
2 CONT [[vincke_lucien_1840]] × [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]] known to have survived to adulthood with no
2 CONT further record of her own (no marriage, no death) — but that is **pure surname-coincidence
2 CONT speculation, not an identifier**, and it is recorded here as exactly that: not a link, not
2 CONT an inference, a bare coincidence noted so a later pass does not rediscover it and
2 CONT overclaim. What would settle it: Constantinus Degraeve's own marriage act, or a Diksmuide
2 CONT or Oostende marriage pairing a Vincke bride to a Degraeve groom. See [[vincke_lucien_1840]]'s
2 CONT own record for the five Vincke children still unaccounted for, any of whom this witness
2 CONT line could equally point to.
