1 FAMC @F195@
1 NOTE Son of [[vincke_lucien_1840]] and [[vanalderweireldt_ludovica_1845]], and [[vincke_emma_1880]]'s brother — one of
2 CONT four children this pass recovers from the couple's **1866-1870 blind window**: the
2 CONT Diksmuide birth index there gives only the bare father surname VINCKE, no forename, no
2 CONT mother, and a birth date recorded as `YYYY/00/00`. His own birth act (Diksmuide 1866 nr.
2 CONT 175) is one of those bare rows, so his parentage comes from his own marriage, 29 years
2 CONT later, not from his birth act.
2 CONT
2 CONT His marriage — Diksmuide, 13 December 1893, act nr. 239 (`rab-bs-huwelijken`) — gives him
2 CONT born Diksmuide 23 July 1866 (matching act nr. 175 exactly), age 27, *schoenmaker*, and
2 CONT names his parents as Vincke Lucien Julien (53, metser) × Vanderweirelt Louise Marie (48,
2 CONT kantwerkster). His own death — Oostende, 22 April 1922, act nr. 280
2 CONT (`rab-bs-overlijdens`) — repeats the parent names (Vincke Lucien Julien × Vanalderweireldt
2 CONT Louise Maria) 29 years later, in a different register and commune, and separately names
2 CONT his surviving spouse, Bolle Valerie Maria, matching the 1893 bride exactly. Full
2 CONT parent-name agreement across two independent registers 29 years apart, plus the
2 CONT death act's own spouse cross-check, is what carries the graft.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The mother's surname on the 1893 act reads VANDERWEIRELT — the "-AL-" dropped — which is
2 CONT why this row is invisible to a query for Vanalderweireldt.** Accepted as the same woman:
2 CONT this pass's own marriage-index sweep queried eight spellings of the surname
2 CONT (Vanalderweireldt, Vanalderweirelt, Vanderweirelt, Vanderweireldt, Alderweireldt,
2 CONT Vanaldeweireldt, Vanalderwerelt, Vandeweireldt) precisely because the family name is
2 CONT transcribed inconsistently across acts, and `Louise`/`Ludovica` is a documented forename
2 CONT fold — `data/forenames.json`'s `f` block groups `ludovica`, `lodewijka` and `louise`
2 CONT together, sex-split so the fold can never cross into a male form.
2 CONT
2 CONT **A rival, ruled out, is the reason this needed care.** A second Diksmuide man,
2 CONT *Theophile Achille Vincke*, son of Adolf Vincke × Celina Maria Vandenberghe, married
2 CONT Delaleeuwe Eugenia in 1903 and died at Diksmuide in 1959
2 CONT (`fwk:e427e82c-0ce3-5a43-afac-4eea747ce86a`) — same forename pair, same surname, same
2 CONT commune. Distinguished by parents, spouse and death year: name and surname alone would
2 CONT have been dangerous here.
2 CONT
2 CONT Index only, not the register image, hence `sup`.
