1 REFN wolf_maria_1836
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Maria /Wolf/
2 GIVN Maria
2 SURN Wolf
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 APR 1836
2 PLAC Brussel
1 OCCU herbergierster (innkeeper)
1 FAMS @F19@
1 FAMC @F225@
1 NOTE Mother of the groom in her son [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 3, 10
2 CONT April 1900 (S28). A *herbergierster* of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe: she kept an inn, as her son's
2 CONT new father-in-law [[thumas_georges_1836]] did at Kraainem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Widowed since 1887 and running the house herself thirteen years later — the act gives her the
2 CONT trade in her own right, not her husband's.
2 CONT
2 CONT **BIRTH DATED, AND A HARD CHILDHOOD NAMED (2026-07-27).** Her own marriage act — Sint-
2 CONT Stevens-Woluwe nr. 4, **17 June 1858** (S33) — gives her birth as **4 April 1836,
2 CONT Brussel**, a *dienstmeyt*, and records her as a *verlaten kind* (abandoned child): she
2 CONT declared under oath that her mother's last residence was unknown to her and that she had
2 CONT never known her, which her witnesses confirmed under oath. The act nonetheless names her
2 CONT mother formally, [[wolf_petronella]], a *dagloonster* — presumably from her own birth
2 CONT record rather than personal knowledge — and names no father for her at all. Both facts are
2 CONT recorded as the act gives them, without resolving one into the other.
2 CONT
2 CONT **The couple's five further children, all read from acts naming this exact birthdate
2 CONT against her stated age, agreeing to the year in five of five:** 21 in 1857
2 CONT ([[bossin_joannes_1857]]), 22 in 1859 ([[bossin_philippus_1859]]), 39 in 1876
2 CONT ([[bossin_jan_1876]]), 46 in 1882 ([[bossin_frans_1882]]), and 43 on
2 CONT [[bossin_ludovicus_1879]]'s own 1879 birth act. See [[bossin_joannes_1834]] for the couple's fuller
2 CONT record, including a sixth child, [[bossin_guillielmus_1869]] (b. Kraainem 1869), known only from
2 CONT his own 1896 marriage act, which also independently restates her husband's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Her surname is spelled five ways across these acts**: *Dewolf* (1857), *Wolf* (1859 and
2 CONT her own 1858 marriage), *Anna Maria De Wolf* (1876), *Wolf* again (1882), *Anna Maria
2 CONT Dewolf* (her son [[bossin_jan_1876]]'s 1897 marriage, age 62) and *Maria Anna Dewolf*
2 CONT ([[bossin_guillielmus_1869]]'s 1896 marriage) — one woman, several clerks, across more than forty
2 CONT years of documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her own trade moves too: *dienstmeyt* at her 1858 marriage, *dagloonster* (1857),
2 CONT unstated (1859), *huishoudster* (1876, 1882, 1897), *herbergierster* in her own right by
2 CONT 1900, after widowhood.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Wolf* is rare enough in this corner of Brabant to be searchable on its own, which is the
2 CONT cheap next move — as is [[wolf_petronella]]'s own record, which names no known husband at
2 CONT all.
1 SOUR @S28@
