1 FAMS @F225@
1 NOTE Named as mother of the bride in her daughter [[wolf_maria_1836]]'s marriage act —
2 CONT Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 4, 17 June 1858 (S33), a *dagloonster*. No father is named for
2 CONT the bride at all — the act records her as a *verlaten kind*, an abandoned child.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Named, but not known to her own daughter.** The same act has [[wolf_maria_1836]] declare
2 CONT under oath that her mother's last residence was unknown to her and that she had never
2 CONT known her, a declaration her witnesses confirmed under oath. Both facts stand as the act
2 CONT gives them: a name and a trade recorded formally, and a daughter who swears she never
2 CONT knew the woman. Neither is resolved into the other here.
2 CONT
2 CONT The act gives no age, so this record carries no birth date.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: whatever record named her to the 1858 clerk in the first place — a foundling
2 CONT register or [[wolf_maria_1836]]'s own birth act — neither yet searched for.
