1 REFN wyllie_brigitte_1779
2 TYPE project-id
1 NAME Brigitte Josephine Joanna /Wyllie/
2 GIVN Brigitte Josephine Joanna
2 SURN Wyllie
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1779
2 PLAC Diksmuide
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 NOV 1824
2 PLAC Diksmuide
1 FAMS @F140@
1 FAMS @F194@
1 NOTE Bore the Scottish-origin surname Wyllie in West-Flanders; widowed young in 1808, remarried
2 CONT in 1818 (below).
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH DATE OPEN, NOT RESOLVED EITHER WAY (2026-07-27). This record held 22 February 1779.
2 CONT Two independent acts — her own 1803 marriage
2 CONT (`data/artifacts/vanalderweireldt-wyllie-1803-marriage-diksmuide.md`) and her 1818
2 CONT remarriage (`data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`) — both instead
2 CONT transcribe her birth as 22 October 1779, the day and month transposed against what was held.
2 CONT Neither reading satisfies both acts' own stated ages, checked by computation: born
2 CONT 22/10/1779 gives age 23 at the 1803 wedding (the act says 24) but age 38 at the 1818 one
2 CONT (the act says 38, correct); born 22/02/1779 gives age 24 in 1803 (correct) but age 39 in
2 CONT 1818 (the act says 38, wrong). Neither candidate is dropped in favour of the other — both
2 CONT are recorded here as competing — so the point date is reduced to the year both
2 CONT transcriptions and the arithmetic agree on. An index-level self-reported age is not primary
2 CONT evidence either way, so even resolving this conflict would not reach `doc`; only her own
2 CONT birth or baptismal record would.
2 CONT
2 CONT REMARRIED, FOUND WITHOUT LOOKING FOR IT (2026-07-27). Diksmuide, 25 June 1818, act nr. 82,
2 CONT RAB ID 85255, microfilm 1166237 (`data/artifacts/looten-wyllie-1818-marriage-diksmuide.md`)
2 CONT — she married [[looten_francois_1785]], a widow at 38. **What identifies this bride as this
2 CONT record is the act's own Previous-Partners table**, not the name agreeing alone: VANALDERWEIRELDT
2 CONT | Antoine | Diksmuide | 06/07/1808 — naming her first husband, his place and a third value
2 CONT for his death day. Her parents are given identically to the 1803 act. The methodological
2 CONT point worth keeping: a Vanalderweireldt-only search would never have found this marriage,
2 CONT because by 1818 she carries a different surname — it surfaced only because her own 1824
2 CONT death act still names Looten as her partner, and the search worked back from there. See
2 CONT [[looten_francois_1785]] for the marriage and the children.
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH DATE CONFIRMED, NOT RETRACTED — A DELIBERATE CONTRAST (2026-07-27). Her own
2 CONT death-index row (Diksmuide act nr. 198, RAB ID 2298609, Certificate Date 10/11/1824, Date
2 CONT column blank) has exactly the same blank-Date-column shape that cost [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]] his
2 CONT day-level precision. Here it does not cost this record anything: both her sons'
2 CONT own 1828 marriage acts — [[vanalderweireldt_carolus_1808]]'s and [[vanalderweireldt_petrus_1803]]'s — independently state
2 CONT her decease as 8 November 1824, this record's held value, a two-day lag behind the
2 CONT certificate date rather than a contradiction of it. Kept at day precision because two later,
2 CONT independent civil acts agree — where Antoine's three sources did not agree with each other
2 CONT at all.
2 CONT
2 CONT FOUR MORE NAMES, NONE LINKED. Her own parents, as both acts name them: **Wyllie François
2 CONT Antoine × Deman** [forename open]. The father leans toward acceptance — named identically
2 CONT in the 1803 and 1818 acts, and corroborated by an exact death date and place (30 September
2 CONT 1811, Diksmuide) given on the 1818 act. Her mother's forename is not settled: the 1803 act
2 CONT writes "Deman Brigitte", the 1818 act "Deman Catharine", and her own death-index row renders
2 CONT her fully as "Deman Catherine Bregite" — read together, this looks like a compound name
2 CONT split differently by different clerks (the same pattern runs through this whole cluster:
2 CONT Isabella Claire/Clara, this record's own Josephine Joanna, Antoine's Joseph Albert), not a
2 CONT contradiction. No single forename is asserted, and neither parent is linked, per the same
2 CONT standard applied on [[vanalderweireldt_antoine_1780]]'s record.
2 CONT
2 CONT TWO MORE GENERATIONS, NAMED AND LEFT OPEN. Her mother's own parents, from her mother's 1801
2 CONT death act (Diksmuide act nr. 48, certificate 1 January 1801): Jean Deman × Marie Jeanne
2 CONT D'Hondt. Her father's own parents, from his 1811 death act (Diksmuide act nr. 175,
2 CONT certificate 2 October 1811): Pierre Jacques Wyllie × Marie Barbe Lengs — the same act
2 CONT recording that he remarried Colette Prudence Minne in 1807, after her mother's death. All
2 CONT four sit one generation beyond an already-open parent generation, on one index row each, and
2 CONT D'Hondt is common enough in this region to carry real rival risk — the same caution §66
2 CONT applied to the Huyghebaert grandparents. Not created as person files, per CLAUDE.md rule 4.
1 SOUR @S126@
